{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_91", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"git diff --check; git status --short; cat cores/bench/implementation_notes.md; python3 -c 'import pathlib; allowed={\\\"cores/bench/rtl/core.sv\\\", \\\"cores/bench/rtl/ex_stage.sv\\\", \\\"cores/bench/rtl/forward_unit.sv\\\", \\\"cores/bench/test/test_pipeline.py\\\"}; import subprocess; changed=set(subprocess.check_output([\\\"git\\\", \\\"diff\\\", \\\"--name-only\\\"], text=True).splitlines()); assert changed == allowed, changed; print(\\\"Only the four authorized RTL/test paths are modified; notes are under cores/bench and gitignored\\\")'\"", "aggregated_output": " M cores/bench/rtl/core.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/ex_stage.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/forward_unit.sv\n M cores/bench/test/test_pipeline.py\n# Implementation\n\nChanged only `rtl/forward_unit.sv`, `rtl/ex_stage.sv`, `rtl/core.sv` and\n`test/test_pipeline.py`.\n\nForwarding now carries three mutually exclusive enables with bit 0 selecting\nID/EX, bit 1 EX/MEM, and bit 2 MEM/WB. EX/MEM retains priority and both writer\nmatches exclude destination x0. MEM/WB eligibility still uses the retained\n`ctrl.reg_write` without qualification by `valid`.\n\nArchitectural rs1/rs2 use three-source masked ORs. ALU A/B use independently\nqualified four-source masked ORs, including PC/immediate directly. Branches,\nJALR, stores and divider RVFI operand capture continue to consume the\narchitectural operands. Pipeline registers, reset/stall/flush/redirect/trap\npriorities, divider latency and arithmetic, ALTOPS and nret=1 are unchanged.\n\nAdded five pipeline cases covering overlapping writers, both mixed-age source\norientations, PC/immediate masking with live encoded sources, x0 destinations,\nforwarded store/branch/JALR, and retained WB forwarding during nine cycles of\ndata backpressure for ADD, ADDI, store, branch, JALR and DIV. The tests check all\nRVFI source addresses/data against independent architectural register state,\nexplicit expected results, contiguous orders, exact retirement PC sequences,\nprivilege/trap fields and exact-once accepted memory effects. Held-WB tests\nalso require forwarding after writeback enable clears.\n\n# Local validation\n\n- Required Verilator lint command: passed without warnings.\n- Complete pytest suite: six runners/proofs passed, including 30 ALU cases,\n  23 pipeline cases, decoder, register file, immediate generator and the real\n  divider's local arithmetic invariant proof.\n- Formal: initial and final runs each passed all 53 ALTOPS checks, zero\n  failures, zero fixes. Final register check completed in 210 seconds.\n  Ran the unchanged `formal/run_all.sh`, `wrapper_si.sv` and `checks_si.cfg`\n  from an isolated copy under `$TMPDI\n…[1616 of 4688 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:fda8c743c44ea8ce]…\nline 28.411 ns, from the\n  register file through ID and EX to divider launch state.\n\n# Deviations and concerns\n\nNo architectural deviation or invalid-payload probe was introduced. The local\nGowin flow mapped equivalent masked-OR term orders differently, so expression\nordering was checked within this same mux rewrite. The selected ALU ORs place\nPC/immediate first, followed by ID/EX, EX/MEM and MEM/WB; the source-enable bit\nmapping remains exactly as specified. Architectural forwarding ORs keep\nID/EX, EX/MEM, MEM/WB order. Continuous assignments express the combinational\nlogic. This local expression ordering improves the final measured median by\n6.70%, exceeding the 4.6% threshold. No correctness concerns remain from the\nlocal gates. Timing sensitivity to equivalent expression grouping is the\nmaterial implementation concern; the final source was rebuilt successfully\nwith all three placement options after selection.\nOnly the four authorized RTL/test paths are modified; notes are under cores/bench and gitignored\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
