{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_22", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"cat formal/checks_si.cfg; sed -n '325,430p' tools/eval/fpga.py; sed -n '1,180p' tools/eval/cosim.py\"", "aggregated_output": "[options]\nisa rv32im\nnret 1\nsolver bitwuzla\n\n[depth]\n# BMC depth per check. 2nd column (where present) is the k-induction prove\n# depth. Keep depths matched to the current pipeline so bugs within ~20\n# cycles of any symbolic instruction stream are exposed.\ninsn          20\nreg       10  20\npc_fwd    10  20\npc_bwd    10  20\ncausal    10  20\n# unique   — no two retirements share rvfi_order (catches double-retire)\n# cover    — sanity that the CPU retires (prevents vacuous-pass suites)\n# ill      — illegal instructions must trap; rvfi_trap from decoder.is_illegal\n# liveness — CPU makes forward progress under any symbolic stream\nunique     1 10 20\ncover      1    20\nill             20\nliveness   1 10 20\n\n[defines]\n`define RISCV_FORMAL_ALIGNED_MEM\n# RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS — fast mode. Same as checks.cfg. See checks.cfg for\n# the full rationale on what ALTOPS does and does not prove. M-extension\n# arithmetic correctness is covered by test/test_alu.py and `make formal-deep`.\n`define RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS\n\n[cover]\n# Sanity cover: the CPU must retire at least one non-trapping instruction.\nalways @* if (!reset) cover (rvfi_valid && !rvfi_trap);\n\n[verilog-files]\n# run_all.sh rebuilds this section from the actual rtl/ glob; the list\n# below is overwritten before genchecks runs. Kept as a placeholder so\n# the section is syntactically present for any reader inspecting the cfg.\n@basedir@/cores/@core@/core.sv\n@basedir@/cores/@core@/wrapper.sv\n    return {'fmax_mhz': summ.get('fmax_mhz'),\n            'pairs': [[r['place_option'], r.get('fmax_mhz'), r.get('levels')] for r in res],\n            'placed': sum(1 for r in res if not r['placement_failed'])}\n\n\ndef run_fpga_eval(worktree: str, target: str | None = None) -> dict:\n    \"\"\"\n    Vendor place-and-route (tools/eval/gowin.py) for Fmax and area, and the\n    Verilator CoreMark run (with random memory stalls) for cycles.\n\n    Returns:\n      {'placement_failed': True, ...}    — the design does not fit or route\n      {'bench_failed': True, ...}        — bench didn't reach ebreak, or\n       \n…[9536 of 12608 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:9f26e4c27d681367]…\nail': 'no ELFs found'}\n\n    # 1. Full-trace cosim of small ELFs (parallel).\n    with ThreadPoolExecutor() as pool:\n        futures = {pool.submit(run_one, elf, sim_bin, worktree, env, flags): elf\n                   for elf in trace_elfs for flags in TRACE_STALL_MODES}\n        for future in as_completed(futures):\n            result = future.result()\n            if not result['passed']:\n                return {\n                    'passed': False,\n                    'failed_elf': result['elf'],\n                    'detail': result,\n                }\n\n    # 2. CoreMark CRC validation (sequential — runs the 500M-cycle sim).\n    if coremark is not None:\n        cm_result = run_coremark_crc(coremark, sim_bin, worktree, env)\n        if not cm_result['passed']:\n            return {\n                'passed': False,\n                'failed_elf': cm_result['elf'],\n                'detail': cm_result,\n            }\n\n    tested = len(trace_elfs) + (1 if coremark else 0)\n    return {'passed': True, 'elfs_tested': tested}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
