{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_55", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'git diff --check; cat cores/bench/implementation_notes.md'", "aggregated_output": "# Parallel radix-16 divider\n\nOnly `rtl/divider.sv` and the allowed arithmetic/pipeline Python tests changed.\nThe divider now consumes one four-bit digit per recurrence edge using fifteen\nindependent 37-bit differences against exact 36-bit divisor multiples. Seven\nodd multiples are registered on the existing second edge from independent\nconstant shift/add or shift/subtract expressions; even multiples are wiring\nshifts of registered state. Monotonic fits produce one-hot choices, balanced\nquotient-bit ORs, and explicit balanced masked-remainder reductions.\n\nPrefix initialization keeps the existing first-nibble Boolean equations and\nuses captured `small4_q` and `small8_q` classifiers. Its second nibble uses\nfifteen parallel nine-bit differences and exact twelve-bit constant multiples,\nwith high-multiple guards before accepting a truncated low-byte comparison.\nClassifier flags reset inactive and remain associated with the captured divisor.\n\nThe edge-one capture, edge-two prefix, and edge-three-through-eight recurrence\nschedule is unchanged. Signed/unsigned zero-divisor behavior, signed overflow,\nsticky completion, consume/relaunch and cancellation are preserved. Multiplier,\npipeline, prediction, forwarding, top-level ports, retirement width, ALTOPS\nformulas, formal configuration/depths, and evaluation sources are unchanged.\n\nTests retain all previous cases and add independent-reference kD boundaries for\nevery radix-16 digit, small-divisor guard transitions, high divisors, signed\ncorners, and 2,048 seeded operand pairs across all four operations. Existing\nedge-eight and sticky-result checks now also verify captured classifier state.\nA pipeline case adds boundary operands with forwarded launch operands and\nmixed MUL/DIV/REM dependencies, exact launch/consume counts and latencies,\nRVFI operands/order, and exact-once stores under simultaneous bus stalls.\n\nLocal validation:\n\n- Verilator `--lint-only -Wall -Wno-MULTITOP`: passed, both real and ALTOPS builds.\n- Unchanged `formal/run_all.sh`, auto-selected single-retire wrapp\n…[1178 of 4250 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:b05be595535e9f14]…\n both ready-high\n  and simultaneous instruction/data stalls (eight trace comparisons).\n- Canonical stalled CoreMark passed UART/CRC and bounds validation and both\n  timing markers: **4,446,945 measured cycles**, unchanged from the champion.\n- Gowin placement options 0/1/2: **66.549 / 71.565 / 71.565 MHz**;\n  median **71.565 MHz**. Option 0 uses **5,430 logic cells, 1,750 registers,\n  zero LUT-RAMs, four BSRAMs, seven DSPs**. Implied fitness is\n  **160.93 iterations/sec**, **11.96% above 143.74**, exceeding the 4.6% gate.\n\nThere are no architectural deviations from the proposed topology. Actual\nvendor timing is below the private prototype's 76.151 MHz median, so that\nprototype frequency is not claimed for this implementation. The measured\nlimiting path moved to forwarded base-ALU execution feeding dmem (option 0:\n20.321 ns through 13 cells). Routing/fanout and the larger arithmetic selection\nremain area/timing considerations. The slow full-core `formal-deep` suite was\nnot run within the implementation budget.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
