ious history.\nAll counter/cache selection stays within its bank; there is no global\nhistory or pattern read and no predictor RAM or target cache.\n\nThe core supplies exactly one accepted update from registered EX/MEM PC,\ninstruction sign, and actual branch direction. Its enable includes valid,\n!reset, !hold_mem_wb, legal branch control, aligned PC, and !instr[8].\nThe existing captured predicted_taken, queue recovery, EX comparison,\nresolved RVFI next PC, nret=1 ports, and memory/replay contracts are retained.\n\nOnly conditional direction selection changes. B/J target arithmetic,\nJAL prediction, sequentia\n…[2275 of 5347 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:4ad372ec60b82cf9]…\nctly 704 registers.\n\nExplicitly simplifying bypass cases worsened the median to 72.504 MHz.\nSharing a local saturation result using A=C[H][1] reduced logic to 6,759\ncells but measured 76.555 / 76.503 / 76.503 MHz. Both explorations passed\ntransition checks; the shared version also passed the full pipeline,\nformal and cosim gates. They do not change predictor behavior or cycles.\n\nFinal fetch wiring and qualification status will be recorded after its\nthree-option placement run and formal gate finish. The main remaining risk\nis physical placement/routing: extra flip-flops and cache/update connectivity\ncan slow existing divider, forwarding, queue and redirect paths even when\nthe predictor's logical fetch depth stays shallow.\ncores/bench/implementation_notes.md\nrg: cores/bench/test/test_pipeline.test_pipeline_runner.None: No such file or directory (os error 2)\nrg: cores/bench/test/results.xml: No such file or directory (os error 2)\nrg: cores/bench/sim_build/core/results.xml: No such file or directory (os error 2)\n", "exit_code": 2, "status": "failed"}}
