{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_52", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261001-001-r10s0.yaml')\nh={\n'id':'hyp-20261001-001-r10s0',\n 'title':'Parallel limb comparisons for radix-16 divider trial selection',\n 'category':'micro_opt',\n 'motivation':'''The champion scores 191.26 iterations/sec at 77.500 MHz and\n4,052,037 marked CoreMark cycles. Its worst path runs from captured\nD bit 1 to prefix remainder bit 7, at 19.241 ns through 22 cells.\nThe r7s0 trial-bank optimization removed serial radix-4 decisions,\nbut each radix-16 fit still waits for a subtraction carry to traverse\nthe complete comparison width before adjacent-fit and remainder\nselection. A local fit/data separation targets that dependency.\nEarlier r8s0 showed that carry-select sum muxes can regress Gowin\nbase-ALU timing, so preserve native subtraction for remainder data.\n''',\n 'hypothesis':'''Separate exact unsigned trial-fit comparison from remainder-data\nsubtraction in both the narrow prefix and the full radix-16 bank.\nFit is T>=kD. Compute it with parallel four-bit limb comparisons and\na balanced lexicographic tree, independently of the native low-result\nsubtraction. Keep the existing nibble Boolean prefix, magnitude-only\nlaunch, eight-bit edge-two initialization, registered odd multiples,\nsix full-width recurrence edges and exact eight-edge completion.\nThis changes one local arithmetic decision structure; no pipeline,\npredictor, issue, memory or arithmetic latency change is proposed.\n\nFor width W=12 or 36, each limb i computes G_i=(X_i>Y_i) and\nE_i=(X_i==Y_i) from its four unsigned bits. Compose a higher and lower\ninterval as G=G_hi|(E_hi&G_lo), E=E_hi&E_lo. Build independent limb\ncomparators, then explicit balanced pair, quad and oct intervals;\ncombine the final high nibble with the lower interval. The final\nunsigned greater-or-equal predicate is G|E. Preserve high-to-low\nordering and exact full widths. Equality must fit, and X=Y=0 must fit.\nAvoid a serial limb loop or a carry-select remainder implementation.\n\nIn the edge-two prefix bank compare {4'b0,T8} against each exact\n12-bit k*D8. Compute only the low eight remainder bits with ordinary\nnative T8-kD8[7:0] subtraction, independently of the fit comparator.\nIn the recurrence compare the full 36-bit T={R,Q[31:28]} against each\nexact registered/shifted 36-bit multiple. Compute only the low 32\nremainder bits with native T[31:0]-multiple[31:0]. This truncation\napplies only to candidate data, never to fit. For a selected trial,\nthe true remainder is at most the consumed dividend prefix and fits\nin 32 bits, so its modular low subtraction is exact. Unselected\nunderflowing results are harmless under the existing one-hot mask.\nKeep fit[0]=1,fit[16]=0, select[k]=fit[k]&&\"'!fit[k+1], and the existing\nbalanced masked-OR remainder and digit reductions. Full exact multiples\nmake fits monotonic. D=0 must select digit 15 and retain the prefix.\n\nKeep every odd-multiple generation/register, signed magnitude and\nresult correction, divide-by-zero/overflow behavior, sticky completion,\nconsume/relaunch rule, reset and M-engine timing unchanged. Preserve\nall ALTOPS expressions and nret=1 ports, decoding, traps, forwarding,\nfetch queuing, memory backpressure and exact-once retirement/effects.\nNo opcode specialization or benchmark-dependent arithmetic is allowed.\n\nProve both limb comparator functions equal native unsigned >= for\narbitrary full-width operands. Retain all existing real-arithmetic\nprefix identities/equivalence, multiple-bank, recurrence, one-hot and\nmonotonic-fit properties without changing their constraints. Retain\nall ALU arithmetic/handshake and pipeline assertions. Add directed\ncomparison equality, limb-boundary borrow, all-zero and all-ones\npatterns, large divisors, signed corners and independent seeded DIV/\nDIVU/REM/REMU references. Run unchanged single-retire formal, full-RVFI\nstalled/unstalled cosim and canonical CoreMark CRC/UART/bounds/markers.\n\nExpect unchanged 4,052,037 measured cycles and improved median Fmax;\nacceptance needs more than approximately 81.066 MHz. Extra comparison\nlogic, limb/tree routing, the still-serial nibble-to-prefix path and\nEX redirect are timing risks. Measure all three vendor placements;\nthe proposed gain is not yet a measured acceptance result.\n'\"''',\n 'expected_impact':{'fitness_delta_pct':8,'confidence':'medium'},\n 'changes':[\n {'file':'rtl/divider.sv','description':'''Add exact balanced unsigned 12/36-bit limb-fit comparators. Use\nthese for both radix-16 trial banks while computing native low\n8/32-bit remainder subtractions in parallel. Retain exact multiple\nwidths, one-hot selection, all state/latency, ALTOPS and handshake.\n'''},\n {'file':'test/test_divider_formal.py','description':'''Add arbitrary-input comparator equivalence properties. Retain every\nexisting real-arithmetic prefix, complete-byte equivalence, registered\nmultiple and recurrence property without weakening constraints.\n'''},\n {'file':'test/test_alu.py','description':'''Retain all arithmetic and per-edge handshake/state assertions;\nadd equality and limb-borrow boundaries, wide divisors, zero and\nsigned extremes with independent exact references.\n'''}]}\np.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(h,sort_keys=False,default_flow_style=False,width=80))\njsonschema.validate(h,json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nprint('Revised hypothesis validates')\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
