{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_77", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261001-001-r10s0.yaml')\nh={\n'id':'hyp-20261001-001-r10s0',\n 'title':'Thermometer-guided balanced muxes for divider remainders',\n 'category':'micro_opt',\n 'motivation':'''The r9s1 champion scores 191.26 iterations/sec at 77.500 MHz and\n4,052,037 marked CoreMark cycles. Its worst vendor path is inside\ndivider prefix initialization: captured divisor bit 1 to remainder\nbit 7, 19.241 ns through 22 cells. The r7s0 micro_opt succeeded by\nfusing both narrow and wide trial banks; selecting their results is\nnow a remaining cost. Current selection computes adjacent-fit one-hot\nbits, masks sixteen data candidates and reduces them through four OR\nlevels. Ordered unsigned multiples already make the fit vector a\nthermometer code, permitting a shorter selection network without any\narithmetic, register, pipeline or instruction-latency change.\n''',\n 'hypothesis':'''Replace only the one-hot masked-OR remainder/digit selection in both\nthe edge-two prefix and full-width radix-16 recurrence with a balanced\nsixteen-leaf mux tree controlled directly by existing trial-fit bits.\nPreserve every subtractor, exact multiple width, Boolean nibble lookup,\nnormalization, register, eight-edge completion and ALTOPS expression.\nThis is one local arithmetic-result selection optimization.\n\nThe current exact trials produce fit[k]=(T>=kD), with fit[0]=1 and\nfit[16]=0. For D>0 the fitting candidates form a contiguous prefix;\nfor D=0 every candidate 0..15 fits. Thus the largest fitting candidate\ncan be chosen by binary partitioning without an adjacent-fit decoder.\nKeep candidate 0's remainder as T, and candidates 1..15 as the low\n8-bit prefix or 32-bit recurrence subtraction result, respectively.\nEach leaf also carries its constant four-bit digit index.\n\nFor pair k, select leaf 2k+1 when fit[2k+1] is true, otherwise leaf 2k.\nFor quad k, select the higher pair when fit[4k+2] is true. For oct k,\nselect the higher quad when fit[8k+4] is true. Select the higher oct\nwhen fit[8] is true. Apply the identical selectors to remainder and\ndigit at every level. All fit predicates are computed in parallel\nby the unchanged trial bank: this is four levels of ordinary two-way\nmuxing, not four serial compare/subtract decisions. Express balanced\nfixed-index wiring explicitly so no priority chain or indexed RAM is\ninferred. Native Gowin mux resources may absorb successive levels.\n\nRemove the old candidate-data masks and OR reductions. Retain or\nre-express the adjacent-fit one-hot signals solely as verification\nmonitors for the existing one-hot/monotonic-fit properties; they must\nnot gate functional remainder or quotient data. Preserve the prefix's\nfinal D>=256 quotient/remainder override, nibble high-divisor guard,\nfull 12/13-bit prefix multiple/subtract widths and full 36/37-bit\nrecurrence widths. D=0 must select leaf 15 and retain T, equality with\nkD must choose k, and T<D must choose zero. No multiple truncation,\nlimb comparator, carry-select adder or initialization retiming is\npart of the delivered hypothesis.\n\nKeep launch/consume, captured operands, sticky result, reset,\nsigned normalization/correction, INT_MIN/-1, divide-by-zero, RVFI,\nnret=1, traps, memory backpressure, forwarding, multiplication and\nfetch behavior unchanged. Preserve every decoder legality and every\narchitectural assertion. All changes stay in bench RTL/unit tests.\n\nProve mux selection equivalent to the former masked-OR selection for\nall monotonic fit patterns and arbitrary candidate payloads, including\nall-fit zero division. Retain all existing real-arithmetic prefix\nidentity/equivalence, exact multiple, recurrence, one-hot and fit-order\nproperties without weakening constraints. Retain arithmetic vectors\nand per-edge state/handshake assertions. Add directed selected-digit\nboundaries kD-1,kD,kD+1 for every k, equality, zero divisors and high-bit\nmultiples; check complete signed/unsigned DIV/REM results independently.\nRun unchanged single-retire formal, full-RVFI stalled/unstalled cosim,\ncanonical CoreMark CRC/UART/bounds/markers and all vendor placements.\n\nExpect unchanged 4,052,037 marked cycles and higher Fmax by removing\nadjacent-fit gating plus a data-mask level ahead of the reduction.\nAcceptance needs median Fmax above about 81.066 MHz. Mux-tree routing,\ncontrol fanout, serial prefix arithmetic and EX redirect may become\nlimits; vendor timing is required before asserting acceptance.\n''',\n 'expected_impact':{'fitness_delta_pct':8,'confidence':'medium'},\n 'changes':[\n {'file':'rtl/divider.sv','description':'''Replace both sixteen-candidate masked-OR result networks with four\nbalanced levels of thermometer-fit-guided muxes for remainder and\ndigit. Retain exact arithmetic, guards, verification monitors, all\nregisters/latency, ALTOPS and launch/consume behavior.\n'''},\n {'file':'test/test_divider_formal.py','description':'''Add arbitrary-payload equivalence of the balanced selector and\noriginal one-hot selector under the exact monotonic-fit condition.\nRetain all production prefix, recurrence and registered-multiple\nproperties with existing constraints and failure behavior.\n'''},\n {'file':'test/test_alu.py','description':'''Retain exact arithmetic, per-edge prefix, eight-edge completion,\nreset and sticky-result assertions. Add all selected-digit equality\nand adjacent boundaries, wide multiples, zero and signed extremes\nwith independent DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU references.\n'''}]}\np.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(h,sort_keys=False,default_flow_style=False,width=80))\njsonschema.validate(h,json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nprint('Final selector hypothesis validates')\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_77", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261001-001-r10s0.yaml')\nh={\n'id':'hyp-20261001-001-r10s0',\n 'title':'Thermometer-guided balanced muxes for divider remainders',\n 'category':'micro_opt',\n 'motivation':'''The r9s1 champion scores 191.26 iterations/sec at 77.500 MHz and\n4,052,037 marked CoreMark cycles. Its worst vendor path is inside\ndivider prefix initialization: captured divisor bit 1 to remainder\nbit 7, 19.241 ns through 22 cells. The r7s0 micro_opt succeeded by\nfusing both narrow and wide trial banks; selecting their results is\nnow a remaining cost. Current selection computes adjacent-fit one-hot\nbits, masks sixteen data candidates and reduces them through four OR\nlevels. Ordered unsigned multiples already make the fit vector a\nthermometer code, permitting a shorter selection network without any\narithmetic, register, pipeline or instruction-latency change.\n''',\n 'hypothesis':'''Replace only the one-hot masked-OR remainder/digit selection in both\nthe edge-two prefix and full-width radix-16 recurrence with a balanced\nsixteen-leaf mux tree controlled directly by existing trial-fit bits.\nPreserve every subtractor, exact multiple width, Boolean nibble lookup,\nnormalization, register, eight-edge completion and ALTOPS expression.\nThis is one local arithmetic-result selection optimization.\n\nThe current exact trials produce fit[k]=(T>=kD), with fit[0]=1 and\nfit[16]=0. For D>0 the fitting candidates form a contiguous prefix;\nfor D=0 every candidate 0..15 fits. Thus the largest fitting candidate\ncan be chosen by binary partitioning without an adjacent-fit decoder.\nKeep candidate 0's remainder as T, and candidates 1..15 as the low\n8-bit prefix or 32-bit recurrence subtraction result, respectively.\nEach leaf also carries its constant four-bit digit index.\n\nFor pair k, select leaf 2k+1 when fit[2k+1] is true, otherwise leaf 2k.\nFor quad k, select the higher pair when fit[4k+2] is true. For oct k,\nselect the higher quad when fit[8k+4] is true. Select the higher oct\nwhen fit[8] is true. Apply the identical selectors to remainder and\ndigit at every level. All fit predicates are computed in parallel\nby the unchanged trial bank: this is four levels of ordinary two-way\nmuxing, not four serial compare/subtract decisions. Express balanced\nfixed-index wiring explicitly so no priority chain or indexed RAM is\ninferred. Native Gowin mux resources may absorb successive levels.\n\nRemove the old candidate-data masks and OR reductions. Retain or\nre-express the adjacent-fit one-hot signals solely as verification\nmonitors for the existing one-hot/monotonic-fit properties; they must\nnot gate functional remainder or quotient data. Preserve the prefix's\nfinal D>=256 quotient/remainder override, nibble high-divisor guard,\nfull 12/13-bit prefix multiple/subtract widths and full 36/37-bit\nrecurrence widths. D=0 must select leaf 15 and retain T, equality with\nkD must choose k, and T<D must choose zero. No multiple truncation,\nlimb comparator, carry-select adder or initialization retiming is\npart of the delivered hypothesis.\n\nKeep launch/consume, captured operands, sticky result, reset,\nsigned normalization/correction, INT_MIN/-1, divide-by-zero, RVFI,\nnret=1, traps, memory backpressure, forwarding, multiplication and\nfetch behavior unchanged. Preserve every decoder legality and every\narchitectural assertion. All changes stay in bench RTL/unit tests.\n\nProve mux selection equivalent to the former masked-OR selection for\nall monotonic fit patterns and arbitrary candidate payloads, including\nall-fit zero division. Retain all existing real-arithmetic prefix\nidentity/equivalence, exact multiple, recurrence, one-hot and fit-order\nproperties without weakening constraints. Retain arithmetic vectors\nand per-edge state/handshake assertions. Add directed selected-digit\nboundaries kD-1,kD,kD+1 for every k, equality, zero divisors and high-bit\nmultiples; check complete signed/unsigned DIV/REM results independently.\nRun unchanged single-retire formal, full-RVFI stalled/unstalled cosim,\ncanonical CoreMark CRC/UART/bounds/markers and all vendor placements.\n\nExpect unchanged 4,052,037 marked cycles and higher Fmax by removing\nadjacent-fit gating plus a data-mask level ahead of the reduction.\nAcceptance needs median Fmax above about 81.066 MHz. Mux-tree routing,\ncontrol fanout, serial prefix arithmetic and EX redirect may become\nlimits; vendor timing is required before asserting acceptance.\n''',\n 'expected_impact':{'fitness_delta_pct':8,'confidence':'medium'},\n 'changes':[\n {'file':'rtl/divider.sv','description':'''Replace both sixteen-candidate masked-OR result networks with four\nbalanced levels of thermometer-fit-guided muxes for remainder and\ndigit. Retain exact arithmetic, guards, verification monitors, all\nregisters/latency, ALTOPS and launch/consume behavior.\n'''},\n {'file':'test/test_divider_formal.py','description':'''Add arbitrary-payload equivalence of the balanced selector and\noriginal one-hot selector under the exact monotonic-fit condition.\nRetain all production prefix, recurrence and registered-multiple\nproperties with existing constraints and failure behavior.\n'''},\n {'file':'test/test_alu.py','description':'''Retain exact arithmetic, per-edge prefix, eight-edge completion,\nreset and sticky-result assertions. Add all selected-digit equality\nand adjacent boundaries, wide multiples, zero and signed extremes\nwith independent DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU references.\n'''}]}\np.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(h,sort_keys=False,default_flow_style=False,width=80))\njsonschema.validate(h,json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nprint('Final selector hypothesis validates')\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "Final selector hypothesis validates\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
