{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_38", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261001-001-r3s0.yaml')\nh=yaml.safe_load(p.read_text())\nh['title']='Parallel one-hot forwarding and ALU operand selection'\nh['motivation']='''The champion scores 98.03 at 44.029 MHz. Its worst path begins at the\nregister file and crosses operand routing, branch resolution, IF and\nhazard logic back to ID. Divider launch is another long live-operand\npath. The failed segmented-divider attempt shows that custom arithmetic\ncarry structures can cost more routing than they save. A temporary probe\nremoving the fetch NOP mux and wide ID bubble clears passed the existing\npipeline suite but reached only 43.818 MHz median, exposing divider launch.\nShorten the operand-selection logic common to both paths instead.\n'''\nh['hypothesis']='''Replace encoded forwarding selects and cascaded data muxes with\nmutually exclusive one-hot source enables and parallel masked-OR\noperand selection. This is one local combinational mux optimization;\nkeep pipeline registers, divider latency, prediction, and bus handling.\n\nFor each EX source, compute M = EX/MEM valid writer, nonzero destination,\nand matching source register; W = MEM/WB ctrl.reg_write, nonzero destination,\nand matching source register. Emit three exclusive source enables:\nID = \"'!M && !W, EXMEM = M, MEMWB = !M && W. Preserve EX/MEM priority and\nx0 behavior exactly. Preserve MEM/WB forwarding without valid qualification:\nits retained payload is required while dmem holds a dependent instruction.\nCarry these three enables directly into EX rather than encoding them\ninto two bits and decoding them again.\n\nSelect architectural rs1 and rs2 with parallel masked ORs over ID/EX,\nEX/MEM, and MEM/WB data. For the ALU operands, qualify those source enables\nwith !is_auipc or !alu_src and add the mutually exclusive PC or immediate\nsource. Select all four candidates in a single parallel expression rather\nthan first constructing the forwarded operand and then applying a second\n32-bit PC/immediate mux. Branch comparisons, JALR and store data must\ncontinue to use architectural forwarded rs1/rs2, while AUIPC and immediate\nALU operations use the qualified ALU masks. Divider operand capture for\nRVFI must still report architectural sources, never substituted PC/imm.\n\nThe expected benefit is less serial select/decode and wide data-mux logic\nbefore branch resolution, ordinary ALU operations, and signed divider\nlaunch normalization. Routing and enable fanout may outweigh the shorter\nlogic, or another path may become limiting. The 12% gain is a timing\nprediction pending vendor measurement; marked CoreMark cycles should stay\nat 4,491,485, and acceptance requires more than 4.6% median fitness gain.\nDo not carry forward the unsuccessful invalid-payload probe.\n\nPreserve every existing reset, stall, flush, redirect, load-use, trap,\nforwarding and retirement priority, the eight-edge divider and ALTOPS\nexpressions, and the nret=1 interface. Validate with the existing pipeline\nand ALU suites, formal and full-trace selftest cosim under both ready-high\nand stalled buses. Add focused cases where EX/MEM and MEM/WB both match a\nsource, different sources need different forwarding ages, x0 is targeted,\nstore/branch/JALR consume forwarded values, and a dependent instruction\nneeds held MEM/WB data during dmem backpressure. Check all RVFI sources,\nresults, contiguous orders and exact-once memory effects. Require canonical\nCoreMark CRCs, UART validation, unchanged marked cycles and median Gowin\nFmax from all three placement options.\n'\"'''\nh['changes']=[\n {'file':'rtl/forward_unit.sv','description':'Emit three mutually exclusive source enables per operand directly from destination-match predicates. Preserve EX/MEM priority, x0 exclusion, and the existing retained MEM/WB forwarding eligibility.'},\n {'file':'rtl/ex_stage.sv','description':'Replace encoded-select case muxes with parallel masked-OR forwarding. Fuse PC/immediate substitution into four-source ALU operand masks so it adds no second wide mux. Keep architectural operands separately for branches, JALR, stores and RVFI; retain all pipeline and divider controls.'},\n {'file':'rtl/core.sv','description':'Widen the two internal forwarding select wires and module connections to carry three one-hot enables. Preserve top-level ports and every pipeline, hazard and RVFI connection.'},\n {'file':'test/test_pipeline.py','description':'Retain all tests and strengthen overlapping-writer priority, both-source forwarding, x0, forwarded branch/store/JALR and held-WB stall cases. Check architectural RVFI operands/results and exact-once retirement/memory side effects.'}]\np.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(h,sort_keys=False,width=88))\nprint(p)\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
