a[27:0],Q} and\n  remainder_q={28'b0,R}. The lookup replaces all four dependent narrow\n  subtract/select stages; do not retain a duplicate restoring network.\n\n  Avoid routing a full 32-bit signed-negation carry chain or normalized\n  divisor high-bit reduction into this bounded l\n…[2330 of 5402 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:fefed3c4c553c4f0]…\ntient/remainder table, raw-operand\n      small-divisor guard and direct signed top-nibble computation. Preserve\n      full magnitude initialization, registered D/3D, all seven busy edges,\n      sign correction, ALTOPS arithmetic and the sticky result handshake.\n  - file: test/test_alu.py\n    description: |\n      Retain all tests and add exhaustive nibble launch cases, signed\n      operands around lower-28-bit zero/carry boundaries, divisors 0,\n      plus/minus 1 through 16, unsigned high-bit divisors and INT_MIN/-1.\n      Check all four real division/remainder operations against independent\n      integer references and preserve existing latency/handshake checks.\n  - file: test/test_divider_formal.py\n    description: |\n      Retain and adapt the launch arithmetic identity and both full-width\n      radix-4 recurrence proofs to the new prefix signals. Prove direct\n      top-nibble normalization and small-divisor classification agree with\n      full unsigned magnitudes for arbitrary raw operands, including zero.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
