asked-OR muxes removes serial operand selection and improves Fmax with unchanged CoreMark cycles, shifting the critical path to divider launch.\n- 2026-10-01 hyp-20261001-002-r3s1 (improvement, +10.05%): Combining explicit flip-flop RF storage with validity-only ID/EX squash removes both BSRAM read-output absorption and redirect feedback through RF addresses and operand capture, improving Fmax with unchanged stalled CoreMark cycles.\n- 2026-10-01 hyp-20261001-001-r4s0 (regression, +11.57%): Boolean nibble quotient/remainder equations plus direct raw-operand normalization remove four dependent launch subtract/select stages and full-width magnitude dependencies, shifting the timing bottleneck to forwarding/ALU-to-memory with unchanged CoreMark cycles.\n- 2026-1\n…[1552 of 4624 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:028c6ffe1defb5cf]…\nject\",\n        \"required\": [\"file\",\"description\"],\n        \"properties\": {\n          \"file\":        {\n            \"type\": \"string\",\n            \"description\": \"Must be under rtl/ (any extension) or be a test/test_*.py cocotb suite. Anything else is rejected by the runtime sandbox check.\",\n            \"pattern\": \"^(rtl/[^.].*|test/test_[^/]+\\\\.py)$\"\n          },\n          \"description\": {\"type\": \"string\"}\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}\nfpga/core_bench_si.sv\nfpga/constraints/Tang_Nano_20K.cst\nfpga/constraints/clock.sdc\nfpga/bench_stall_gen.sv\nfpga/core_bench.sv\nfpga/scripts/synth.tcl\nfpga/scripts/nextpnr_run.sh\ncores/bench/test/test_imm_gen.py\ncores/bench/test/conftest.py\ncores/bench/test/test_pipeline.py\ncores/bench/test/_helpers.py\ncores/bench/test/test_branch_predictor.py\ncores/bench/test/test_decoder.py\ncores/bench/test/test_divider_formal.py\ncores/bench/test/test_reg_file.py\ncores/bench/test/test_id_stage.py\ncores/bench/test/test_alu.py\ncores/bench/experiments/progress.png\ncores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
