{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_29", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261001-001-r5s0.yaml'", "aggregated_output": "id: hyp-20261001-001-r5s0\ntitle: \"Prepare divider launch operands before forwarding selection\"\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  The champion scores 121.32 at 51.680 MHz with 4,259,699 marked\n  CoreMark cycles. Its 24.772 ns worst path starts at EX/MEM destination\n  metadata and crosses forwarding into the divider launch remainder.\n  Prior micro_opt attempts tried carry-select subtraction, parallel\n  operand muxes, and Boolean launch-prefix arithmetic. They show that\n  forwarding control followed by arithmetic is costly, and that removing\n  divider launch exposes the multiplier-to-memory path. Target the\n  serial dependence of launch preparation on forwarding arbitration.\nhypothesis: |\n  Speculatively prepare divider launch arithmetic for each of the three\n  existing forwarding candidates, then select the prepared values with\n  the existing youngest-writer priority. This is a local combinational\n  scheduling optimization: move signed magnitude conversion and divisor\n  multiple generation before the forwarding data mux. Keep every stage,\n  the four-bit launch prefix, seven registered recurrence edges, and the\n  exact eight-edge divider latency unchanged.\n\n  For each candidate source word X, independently form its 32-bit\n  magnitude M = signed_division && X[31] ? -X : X, where signed_division\n  means DIV or REM. Prepare the dividend candidates from ID/EX rs1_val,\n  EX/MEM alu_result, and the actual WB write-data mux output. Prepare the\n  divisor candidates from the corresponding rs2 sources. For each divisor\n  magnitude, also compute 3M as a full 34-bit unsigned value. Select the\n  prepared dividend magnitude, divisor magnitude, and 3M using identical\n  source enables to architectural rs1/rs2 forwarding. Thus destination\n  comparison and forwarding priority run in parallel with normalization\n  and multiple generation instead of preceding their carry chains.\n  Use one mutually exclusive masked-OR selection per prepared output;\n  do not put another magnitude conversion or 3D addition after selection.\n\n  EX/MEM must\n…[3574 of 6646 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:898797f6efef8268]…\nfter selection. Keep a standalone\n      fallback and preserve all recurrence, sign, latency and handshake\n      behavior in real and ALTOPS builds.\n  - file: test/test_alu.py\n    description: |\n      Retain all tests and exercise both raw and prepared launch modes\n      against independent RV32M references, including signed overflow,\n      zero/high-bit divisors, busy input changes and held completions.\n  - file: test/test_divider_formal.py\n    description: |\n      Preserve all arithmetic assertions and extend the local proof to\n      show selected prepared magnitudes/3D equal raw-input preparation,\n      including 34-bit multiple bounds and signed/zero corner cases.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: |\n      Retain existing tests and strengthen forwarding-source combinations,\n      overlapping-writer priority, forwarded loads and retained WB across\n      stalls. Check exact RVFI operands/results, latency, retirement order\n      and exact-once memory effects for dependent and chained divisions.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
