{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_7", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfor line in Path('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl').read_text().splitlines():\n e=json.loads(line)\n if e['category']=='micro_opt':\n  print('\\\\nID:',e['id'],'TITLE:',e['title'],'FITNESS:',e.get('fitness'),'OUTCOME:',e['outcome'])\n  print('PATH:',e.get('critical_path'))\n  h=e.get('hypothesis',{})\n  if isinstance(h,dict): print('PROPOSAL:',h.get('hypothesis',''))\n  print('NOTES:',e.get('implementation_notes',''))\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "\nID: baseline-bench-fdef707 TITLE: Baseline retest for cores/bench FITNESS: 12.12 OUTCOME: improvement\nPATH: {'from': 'cpu/u_mem/reg_q.rd_3_s0', 'to': 'dmem_0_dmem_0_0_0_s', 'slack_ns': -189.542, 'arrival_ns': 199.837, 'logic_cells': 156, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_fwd', 'cpu/u_ex', 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu', 'cpu/u_ex']}\nPROPOSAL: \nNOTES: \n\nID: hyp-20261001-001-r1s0 TITLE: Shared combinational radix-4 division with parallel trial subtracts FITNESS: 12.65 OUTCOME: regression\nPATH: {'from': 'cpu/u_mem/reg_q.rd_1_s0', 'to': 'cpu/u_ex/reg_q.alu_result_18_s0', 'slack_ns': -175.376, 'arrival_ns': 185.67, 'logic_cells': 249, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_fwd', 'cpu/u_ex', 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu', 'cpu/u_ex']}\nPROPOSAL: Replace only the real DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU datapath with one combinational\nunsigned radix-4 restoring divider, shared by all four operations. Keep\nthe ALU interface, execution latency, pipeline, forwarding, bus-stall\nbehavior, and nret=1 port contract unchanged. Convert signed operands\nto unsigned 32-bit magnitudes before the divider and correct quotient\nand remainder signs afterward; unsigned operations use operands directly.\n\nUnroll 16 stages, each consuming two dividend bits. Precompute D, 2D,\nand 3D once as 34-bit unsigned values. Each stage forms T=4*R+next_two_bits and\ncomputes T-D, T-2D, and T-3D in parallel. Derive the three fit predicates\nfrom the extended subtract results' borrow bits, rather than adding\nseparate magnitude comparisons. Select the largest fitting multiple\nwith a small priority encoder and a balanced four-way remainder mux,\nand append its two-bit quotient digit. Taper stage widths to the consumed\ndividend prefix: stage i, numbered from zero, needs W=2*(i+1) bits for\nT and its remainder. Subtract the low W bits of each multiple using\nW+1 bits; a candidate fits only if its borrow is zero AND every bit of\nthat 34-bit multiple above W-1 is zero. This high-bit guard is mandatory,\nespecially for divisors near UINT_MAX; truncating multiples without it\nis incorrect. The width bound follows from th\n…[24234 of 27306 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:3d19cfe714a93e68]…\nnt pipeline state and retained WB eligibility. Exercise\nall source ages, simultaneous matching writers, independent sources,\nx0, loads and load-use bubbles, misaligned producer suppression, killed\nyounger instructions, divide launch/drain/consume, dmem holds before\nand after divide completion, and reset. Check architectural RVFI\noperands/results, order, PC continuity and memory side effects under\nready-high and randomized instruction/data bus backpressure.\n\nVerify with unchanged pipeline and ALU tests, local divider arithmetic\nproof, full single-retire formal gate and canonical stalled CoreMark\ncosim. Expect exactly the champion's marked cycles, with improved\nmedian Gowin Fmax from the shorter forwarding control path. Acceptance\nabove 121.32 requires roughly 54.06 MHz at those cycles. Data-driven\ndivider launch, multiplication, or match-register placement may limit\nthe gain; use all three vendor placement options. The timing gain is\nan unmeasured prediction until the prototype/evaluator confirms it.\n\nNOTES: \n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
