arding-to-ALU critical path, limiting Fmax improvement to 4.37% with unchanged CoreMark cycles.\"\n}\n{\n  \"id\": \"hyp-20261001-001-r2s0\",\n  \"title\": \"Segmented carry-select subtractors for the eight-edge divider\",\n  \"outcome\": \"regression\",\n  \"fitness\": 58.46,\n  \"fmax_mhz\": 26.259,\n  \"cycles\": 4491485,\n  \"critical_path\": {\n    \"from\": \"cpu/u_rf/regs_regs_0_0_s0\",\n    \"to\": \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu/u_divider/quotient_q_0_s0\",\n    \"slack_ns\": -33.341,\n    \"arrival_ns\": 43.636,\n    \"logic_cells\": 50,\n    \"modules\": [\n      \"clock_ibuf\",\n      \"cpu/u_id\",\n      \"cpu/u_ex\",\n      \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu/u_divider\",\n      \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu/u_divider/g_trial[0].u_subtractor\",\n      \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu/u_divider\",\n      \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu/u_divider/g_trial[1].u_subtractor\",\n      \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu/u_divider\",\n      \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu/u_divider/g_trial[\n…[11304 of 14376 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:c0b644789f09ff69]…\nons with parallel D/2D/3D trials and raw-operand nibble normalization shorten the divider cone without added BSRAM or CoreMark cycles; six-bit multiples and high-bit fit guards prevent truncated multiples from falsely fitting.\"\n}\n{\n  \"id\": \"hyp-20261001-001-r7s0\",\n  \"title\": \"Fuse narrow and full-width divider digit pairs\",\n  \"outcome\": \"improvement\",\n  \"fitness\": 165.86,\n  \"fmax_mhz\": 73.757,\n  \"cycles\": 4446945,\n  \"critical_path\": {\n    \"from\": \"cpu/u_id/reg_q.rs1_val_14_s0\",\n    \"to\": \"dmem_3_dmem_3_0_0_s\",\n    \"slack_ns\": -9.71,\n    \"arrival_ns\": 20.005,\n    \"logic_cells\": 13,\n    \"modules\": [\n      \"clock_ibuf\",\n      \"cpu/u_ex\",\n      \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu\",\n      \"cpu/u_ex\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"lesson\": \"- 2026-10-01 hyp-20261001-001-r7s0 (improvement, +15.39%): Parallel radix-16 trial banks must cover both the narrow initialization prefix and full-width divider recurrence to remove serial subtract/select bottlenecks and raise Fmax at