{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_80", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport json,yaml,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261001-001-r8s0.yaml')\nh={\n'id':'hyp-20261001-001-r8s0',\n'title':'Four-bit parallel carry lookahead for base ALU arithmetic',\n'category':'micro_opt',\n'motivation':'''The champion scores 165.86 iterations/sec at 73.757 MHz with 4,446,945 marked CoreMark cycles. Its worst reported path is 20.005 ns through thirteen cells from ID/EX rs1 through EX/base ALU to dmem. Round 7 removed serial divider decisions, exposing ordinary forwarded address arithmetic. The prior round-2 micro_opt used eight-bit carry-select blocks inside four serial divider steps and regressed to 26.259 MHz; its launch/selection chain remained critical. Instead optimize only the single base-ALU addition or subtraction per instruction, using shorter four-bit blocks and parallel logarithmic carry prefix. Leave the now successful divider untouched.''',\n'hypothesis':'''Replace the real base ALU ADD and SUB expressions with one reusable 32-bit modulo adder function made from eight parallel four-bit blocks, a balanced three-level block carry-prefix network, and local carry-select result muxes. ADD invokes it with x=a,y=b,cin=0; SUB invokes it with x=a,y=~b,cin=1. Do not share their operation-controlled operand inversion ahead of ADD, since loads/stores always use ADD and should not acquire another late control mux. Keep all ALU encodings, combinational interfaces and instruction latencies unchanged.\n\nFor block k compute two independent exact five-bit sums S0[k]={0,x[4k+:4]}+{0,y[4k+:4]} and S1[k]={0,x[4k+:4]}+{0,y[4k+:4]}+1. These are parallel short native carry chains, never sums of previously selected blocks. Set G[k]=S0[k][4] and P[k]=&(S0[k][3:0]). P from the low sum is correct: when those four bits are all ones, carry-in can carry through the block; if G is already one its value dominates regardless of P. Fold cin into G[0] as G[0]|(P[0]&cin).\n\nBuild explicit prefix levels at strides 1,2,4. At each level and each k at least the stride, combine only the previous level: G_next[k]=G_prev[k]|(P_prev[k]&G_prev[k-stride]), P_next[k]=P_prev[k]&P_prev[k-stride]; otherwise copy that group. Carry into block zero is cin, and carry into block k>0 is the final prefix G[k-1]. Select S1[k][3:0] or S0[k][3:0] with that carry. Discard final carry, retaining exact 32-bit wraparound. Do not introduce a serial eight-block carry recurrence, a full-width increment after a chosen sum, or a second full-width ripple adder in parallel.\n\nThis changes only the combinational base ADD/SUB implementation. Preserve every existing multiply/divide expression and ALTOPS formula, both M-engine handshakes and latencies, launch operand capture, forwarding, branch arithmetic, PC arithmetic, decode legality, stage payloads, stalls, traps and nret=1 IO. In particular do not apply this helper to the divider or change its radix-16 prefix/recurrence. The desired gain is shorter carry propagation on the observed ALU/address path at identical marked cycles; increased LUTs, local mux delay and newly limiting divider/redirect paths are risks.\n\nProve the helper equals (x+y+cin) modulo 2\"'^32 for arbitrary operands and both carry inputs using a local combinational SAT property without touching the shared formal wrapper/configuration. Add independent ADD/SUB references with seeded random values and directed carry propagation through consecutive all-ones four-bit block sums, carry-generate/kill patterns at every nibble boundary, borrow across bit 31 and unsigned wraparound. Retain all existing arithmetic and pipeline assertions. Run the unchanged single-retire formal checks, stalled/unstalled full-trace cosim and canonical stalled CoreMark with all CRC/UART/bounds/marker gates. Expect exactly 4,446,945 marked cycles; acceptance at unchanged cycles needs median vendor Fmax above 77.150 MHz. Measure all three Gowin placement options. The expected gain is a timing hypothesis, not a claim that the acceptance gate has already passed.'\"''',\n'expected_impact':{'fitness_delta_pct':7,'confidence':'medium'},\n'changes':[\n {'file':'rtl/alu.sv','description':'Implement exact eight-by-four-bit parallel carry-select addition with three logarithmic prefix levels for base ADD and SUB only. Preserve all other arithmetic, interfaces, M engines and ALTOPS formulas.'},\n {'file':'test/test_alu.py','description':'Retain all existing tests and add independent ADD/SUB carry/borrow boundary vectors plus deterministic random comparisons, including both signed bit patterns and modulo wraparound.'},\n {'file':'test/test_adder_formal.py','description':'Add a local combinational SAT equivalence property for the helper against independent full-width x+y+cin modulo arithmetic, both carry inputs and arbitrary 32-bit operands. Keep every shared formal/evaluation contract unchanged.'}\n]}\np.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(h,sort_keys=False,width=90))\njsonschema.validate(h,json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nprint('Final focused hypothesis is schema-valid:',p)\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
