{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_18", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfor r in map(json.loads,Path('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl').read_text().splitlines()):\n if r['id'].endswith('r7s0'):\n  print('hypothesis:', r['hypothesis']['hypothesis'])\n  print('notes:',r.get('implementation_notes',''))\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "hypothesis: Fuse each pair of radix-4 digit decisions inside the real divider into\none parallel radix-16 trial bank. Apply the same arithmetic optimization\nto the final four bits of the edge-2 initialization prefix and to every\nfour-bit recurrence on edges 3 through 8. This is a local\narithmetic reorganization inside divider.sv, not a change to pipeline\ntopology, fetch prediction, issue width, or the M-engine handshake.\nKeep edge 1 magnitude capture and edge 2 eight-bit prefix initialization,\nand still consume exactly four dividend bits on each subsequent edge.\nCompletion must remain on edge eight with the existing sticky result.\n\nFirst eliminate the serial narrow decisions in edge 2. Retain the\nexisting explicit Boolean nibble truth functions, but evaluate this\nhelper against D8=D[7:0]. Its nibble override tests D8[7:4], rather\nthan propagating D[31:8] through the arithmetic chain. Form the\neight-bit T8={nibble_remainder,A[27:24]}. Compute all k*D8 multiples\nexactly at 12 unsigned bits for k=1..15, using shifted D8, independent\nodd-multiple sums and carry-save compression for three-term sums.\nEvaluate thirteen-bit zero-extended T8-k*D8 trials in parallel, derive\nadjacent-fit one-hot selectors, and use balanced masked-OR trees for\nthe eight-bit remainder and four-bit digit. Concatenate the Boolean\nnibble quotient and the new digit into Q_prefix. Qualify the complete\nbyte-prefix result once at the final output: if D[31:8]!=0, force\nQ_prefix=0 and R_prefix=A[31:24]; otherwise use the computed result.\nThis is exact because any D