e registered D, 3D, 5D, and 7D. Edge two's prefix trial bank must\n  read these registers exclusively, removing every combinational\n  odd-multiple-generation adder from its subtract/select cone.\n\n  Keep twelve-bit multiples and thirteen-bit extended trial differences\n  so that 1\n…[1911 of 4983 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:b2fc90b4810a6fe2]…\n rtl/divider.sv\n    description: |\n      Add seven launch-captured twelve-bit odd multiples of the independently\n      normalized low divisor byte. Drive the existing prefix trial bank\n      from these registers and constant shifts. Keep all widths, guards,\n      full-width recurrence, edge count, handshake and ALTOPS behavior.\n  - file: test/test_divider_formal.py\n    description: |\n      Prove captured prefix multiples equal exact multiples of the stored\n      divisor byte after accepted launch. Preserve arithmetic identities,\n      byte-prefix equivalence and recurrence proofs, accounting explicitly\n      for the new registered-bank consistency in combinational abstractions.\n  - file: test/test_alu.py\n    description: |\n      Retain all arithmetic and handshake tests. Add exhaustive byte-prefix\n      quotient/remainder comparisons and full-operation cases for signed\n      byte-normalization carries, D>=256, zero, overflow, operand changes\n      while busy, held completion, reset and back-to-back requests.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
