{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_46", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml, json, jsonschema\npath = Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261001-002-r3s1.yaml')\ndata = {\n'id': 'hyp-20261001-002-r3s1',\n'title': 'Explicit banked register file with balanced one-hot reads',\n'category': 'structural',\n'motivation': '''The champion reaches 44.029 MHz and 98.03 fitness with 4,491,485\nmarker-bracketed CoreMark cycles after separating divider launch from\niteration. Its reported worst path starts in register-file storage and\npasses through ID, EX, IF and hazard logic to an ID/EX operand register.\nPrior structural wins attacked division, and the predictor experiments\nshow that modest cycle savings lose when operand delivery limits Fmax.\nA temporary vendor-timed probe confirms that Gowin implements the\narray-style register file in BSRAM and absorbs operand pipeline storage\ninto RAM read outputs. Its operand path starts at a BSRAM DO pin with\n2.260 ns clock-to-output delay, then reaches EX logic directly. Replacing\nthis small storage structure can improve the same operand-delivery\nboundary without adding instruction latency or changing arithmetic.\n''',\n'hypothesis': '''Replace only the integer register-file storage and read topology with\n31 individually declared 32-bit flip-flop words arranged as four groups\nof eight register numbers. x0 occupies a constant-zero slot and has no\nstorage. Give each nonzero word its own synchronous reset and decoded\nwrite enable. Preserve the single synchronous architectural write port\nand the two combinational read ports, including existing write-first\nbypass and x0 priority. Keep the champion pipeline, branch policy,\nhazard/forwarding protocol and eight-edge divider unchanged.\n\nFor each read port, predecode its five-bit source index into shared\none-hot word selects. AND each word with its select, reduce the eight\nmasked words in each group using a balanced OR tree, then reduce the\nfour group results with another balanced tree. Use explicit generated\nword registers and fixed-index wiring for both reads and writes; avoid\na variable-indexed array template that can be recognized as RAM.\nBalance reductions explicitly rather than using a serial accumulator.\nThe four groups are a physical read-network organization, not access\nbanks: both ports must read any pair of words in the same cycle,\nincluding two words in the same group, with no conflicts or stalls.\nUse portable SystemVerilog constant indices and existing tool-supported\nconstructs; vendor primitives or timing exceptions are unnecessary.\n\nThe structural claim is that a flip-flop source bank plus a shallow\nread network restores a distinct ID/EX operand capture boundary and\nremoves slow BSRAM read-output launches into the EX branch/divider path.\nDo not insert new stages or register read outputs inside reg_file.\nLeave ID/EX timing and its functional enable/reset behavior unchanged.\nCheck the vendor netlist and timing report for elimination of register\nfile BSRAM instances and actual ID/EX operand flip-flops; accept the\nhypothesis by measured fitness, not merely by desired RAM inference.\nThis trades about 992 storage flip-flops and extra read-selection LUTs\nfor shorter operand paths, using the substantial remaining FPGA area.\nHigh-fanout select/write nets, placement congestion, and a new divider\nrecurrence bottleneck are the principal risks. Target a material Fmax\ngain with exactly unchanged CoreMark iterations/cycle.\n\nPreserve synchronous reset clearing every architectural register,\nx0 hardwiring even on same-cycle writes, write-first forwarding on\nboth read ports, and isolation of unwritten registers. Preserve nret=1,\nall core ports, exact-once in-order retirement, retained MEM/WB bypass\nunder memory stalls, decoder default-illegal and alignment traps,\nRV32M bit results and ALTOPS formulas. Preserve the ready-high ten-clock\nbranch-to-divide successor bound. Do not change any eval or formal\ncontract. Validate the register-file unit tests, all existing pipeline\ntests, formal, and marker-bracketed stalled canonical CoreMark with\nall CRCs and validation text. Add all-address and same-group read tests,\nreset-after-writes, x0 bypass priority, and alternating same-cycle writes\non each port. Judge median Gowin Fmax times iterations/cycle against\n98.03, requiring more than a 4.6% gain. The expected improvement is a\nhypothesis until the full placement median and correctness gates pass.\n''',\n'expected_impact': {'fitness_delta_pct': 15, 'confidence': 'medium'},\n'changes': [\n {'file': 'rtl/reg_file.sv', 'description': '''Replace the dynamically indexed register array with 31 independent\n32-bit synchronous-reset flip-flop words and constant x0. Implement\ntwo shared one-hot source decoders and balanced four-by-eight masked\nOR read networks, with independently decoded synchronous writes.\nPreserve the current combinational write-first bypass and interface.\nPrevent RAM/output-register absorption through the explicit storage\nand fixed-index read topology; add no cycles or bank conflicts.\n'''},\n {'file': 'test/test_reg_file.py', 'description': '''Retain every existing assertion. Extend coverage to all 31 writable\nregisters and all source-pair combinations, both ports reading the\nsame register or same group, writes that alias either or both read\nports, x0 priority, unwritten-register isolation, and synchronous\nreset after nonzero writes. Use an independent architectural-array\nreference for seeded mixed read/write sequences.\n'''},\n {'file': 'test/test_pipeline.py', 'description': '''Retain every existing pipeline and arithmetic check, including the\nten-clock branch-to-divide bound. Add same-group operand dependencies\nand source/destination aliases through EX/MEM and retained MEM/WB\nforwarding under simultaneous randomized imem/dmem stalls. Verify\nRVFI operands, results, PC chains, contiguous order and exact-once\nmemory side effects without modifying the harness.\n'''}]\n}\ntext = yaml.safe_dump(data, sort_keys=False, width=76)\njsonschema.validate(yaml.safe_load(text), json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\npath.write_text(text)\nprint('Revised structural hypothesis written and schema-validated.')\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
