it all effect and hazard enables against their stage'\"'s valid bit.\nArbitrary invalid payloads must not launch division, redirect, issue\nmemory requests, write registers, create dependencies or retire. The\nexisting MEM/WB bypass deliberately survives WB.valid clearing on a\nmemory stall: preserve that retained result/destination behavior. On a\nnormal MEM/WB capture, qualify its stored reg_write/bypass eligibility\nwith EX/MEM.valid and existing trap suppression, so an invalid writing\nopcode cannot become a false bypass. During hold_wb, retain data, tag\nand eligibility and clear only retirement valid, exactly as before.\nDo not simply gate MEM/WB bypass by retirement valid.\n\nThis spends about 992 RF storage flip-flops plus read-selection LUTs to\nremove both measured operand-delivery limits without extra instruction\ncycles. High-fanout decode/write nets, placement congestion and the\nregistered divider recurrence are the principal remaining timing risks.\nKeep nret=1, every core port, decoder default-illegal rules, alignment\ntraps, RV32M arithmetic and ALTOPS formulas, contiguous in-order RVFI\nretirement, exact-once memory effects, and the ready-high ten-clock\nbranch-to-divide successor bound. Change no eval or formal contracts.\n\nRun unchanged unit tests, formal and canonical stalled CoreMark; extend\nRF all-address/same-group/bypass/reset tests and adversarial invalid\npayload tests. Cover killed loads, stores, divides, jumps, illegal\ninstructions and writes aliasing live operands, along with load-use\nreplay and retained WB bypass during prolonged memory stalls. Check\nall canonical CRCs and validation text, compare marker-bracketed cycles\nto 4,491,485, and inspect timing for elimination of both RF BSRAM launches\nand redirect-to-read-address feedback. Accept only median vendor Gowin\nFmax times iterations/cycle more than 4.6% above 98.03. Prototype\nmeasurements do not replace the full formal and evaluator gates.\n'''\nexisting={x['file']:x for x in d['changes']}\nd['changes']=[existing['rtl/reg_file.sv'],\n {'file':'rtl/if_stage.sv','description':'''Expose raw fetched instruction and PC to decode, with fetch validity\nfrom imemReady independently of squash. Remove the redirect/flush NOP\nmux and retain PC hold and accepted-redirect priority. Add no stage.\n'''},\n {'file':'rtl/id_stage.sv','description':'''Split wide ID/EX payload capture from validity update. Capture payload\non every edge not held by downstream dmem/divider backpressure, while\nload-use/redirect only invalidate the new slot. Retain both on a true\nhold and preserve reset. Keep raw source fields independent of kill.\n'''},\n {'file':'rtl/hazard_unit.sv','description':'''Separate true downstream hold from younger-slot kill. Load-use still\nholds fetch PC and creates a bubble but does not hold payload storage.\nUse ready-qualified raw source fields for hazard comparisons and keep\nmemory/divider/redirect advancement priorities unchanged.\n'''},\n {'file':'rtl/core.sv','description':'''Connect ready-qualified fetch validity and separate ID hold/kill\nsignals. Audit valid qualification of hazards and side effects while\npreserving divider wiring, stage boundaries, nret=1 ports and RVFI.\n'''},\n {'file':'rtl/mem_stage.sv','description':'''Qualify captured MEM/WB reg_write/bypass eligibility with EX/MEM.valid\nand trap suppression on normal captures, preventing invalid payloads\nfrom forwarding false writes. Retain prior data, tag and eligibility\non hold_wb while clearing only retirement validity, as before.\n'''},\n existing['test/test_reg_file.py'],\n {'file':'test/test_pipeline.py','description':'''Retain every existing check, including the ten-clock branch-to-divide\nbound. Add same-group operands, invalid-payload live-register aliases,\nwrong-path loads/stores/divides/jumps/illegal instructions, load-use\nreplay, and retained WB forwarding across prolonged memory holds under\nrandomized bus stalls. Check RVFI operands, PC chains, contiguous order\nand exact-once accepted memory effects without modifying the harness.\n'''}]\nclass BlockDumper(yaml.SafeDumper): pass\ndef represent_str(dumper,value):\n    return dumper.represent_scalar('tag:yaml.org,2002:str',value,style='|' if '\\\\n' in value else None)\nBlockDumper.add_representer(str,represent_str)\ns=yaml.dump(d,Dumper=BlockDumper,sort_keys=False,width=76)\njsonschema.validate(yaml.safe_load(s),json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\np.write_text(s)\nprint('Combined operand-boundary hypothesis written and validated.')\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "Combined operand-boundary hypothesis written and validated.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
