 already captured with each accepted fetch, never\n  recompute its prediction from current state. Delayed updates and aliases\n  affect accuracy only. Preserve occupancy-only queue recovery, validity-only\n  kills, accepted correction priority, bus handshakes, forwarding, load-use\n  and multiply replay, M arithmetic/ALTOPS, decoder legality, alignment traps,\n  nret=1 ports, resolved architectural RVFI next PC and contiguous retirement.\n\n  Verify all counter states against independent saturating integer arithmetic,\n  every history transition, same-context bypass, unchanged future-context\n  selection, same-bank aliases, consecutive registered updates, no update on\n  holds, reset, and cold static behavior. Retain exhaustive B/J target and\n  reserved-encoding checks. Pipeline cases must combine changing predictor\n  state with queued instructions, loop exits, forward branches, every existing\n  hold reason and wrong-path stores, checking full RVFI PCs, operands, order\n  and exact-once memory effects. Run unchanged lint, formal and cosim gates,\n  canonical bracketed CoreMark CRC/UART/OOB validation and all three Gowin\n  placement options. Qualification requires fitness above 200.058 iter/sec;\n  increased FF placement density and cached-update routing are the main risks.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/branch_predictor.sv\n    description: \\\"Add 64 fixed local-history banks with four agreement counters and a cached next agreement bit per bank; use local parallel training, exact same-context update forwarding, Boolean saturating transitions and a shallow cached-bit fetch lookup. Preserve B/J targets and legal/aligned control guards.\\\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \\\"Wire predictor clock/reset and one accepted training event from existing registered EX/MEM PC, instruction, branch_taken and post-trap validity. Preserve every pipeline bundle, top-level port and retirement contract.\\\"\n  - file: test/test_branch_predictor.py\n    description: \\\"Retain exhaustive direct target, legality and alignment checks; add an independent history/counter/cache model for every state transition, same-context bypass, aliases, consecutive updates, holds and reset.\\\"\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: \\\"Preserve architectural assertions and check prediction state changes behind queued fetches, all hold reasons, loop exits, forward branches, RVFI continuity and absence of wrong-path stores.\\\"\n''')\nprint(p)\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261001-003-r10s2.yaml\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
