{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/LESSONS.md schemas/hypothesis.schema.json'","aggregated_output":"- 2026-10-01 hyp-20261001-001-r1s0 (regression, +4.37%): Sharing DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU in a tapered radix-4 divider reduced logic cells by 60%, but parallel trial-subtract selection and routing kept division on the forwarding-to-ALU critical path, limiting Fmax improvement to 4.37% with unchanged CoreMark cycles.\n- 2026-10-01 hyp-20261001-002-r1s1 (improvement, +522.03%): A shared eight-edge divider with four restoring steps per clock breaks the combinational / and % chain feeding the EX result mux, making the Fmax gain outweigh blocking DIV/REM latency in CoreMark.\n- 2026-10-01 hyp-20261001-002-r2s1 (improvement, +30.03%): Separating a four-bit launch prefix with high-divisor guards from two radix-4 stages fed by registered D/3D multiples improves divider timing by removing live-operand muxing and halving serial full-width subtract/select decisions while retaining eight-edge latency.\n- 2026-10-01 hyp-20261001-003-r2s2 (regression, +16.21%): A 64-entry direction table with decoded B/J targets cuts stalled CoreMark cycles by 6.45%, but the register-file-to-divider launch path remains critical, so its throughput gain trails retiming that path.\n- 2026-10-01 hyp-20261001-001-r3s0 (regression, +6.69%): Combining forwarding and PC/immediate selection in parallel one-hot masked-OR muxes removes serial operand selection and improves Fmax with unchanged CoreMark cycles, shifting the critical path to divider launch.\n- 2026-10-01 hyp-20261001-002-r3s1 (improvement, +10.05%): Combining explicit flip-flop RF storage with validity-only ID/EX squash removes both BSRAM read-output absorption and redirect feedback through RF addresses and operand capture, improving Fmax with unchanged stalled CoreMark cycles.\n{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"required\": [\"id\",\"title\",\"category\",\"motivation\",\"hypothesis\",\"expected_impact\",\"changes\"],\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"id\":       {\"type\": \"string\", \"pattern\": \"^hyp-[0-9]{8}-[0-9]{3}(-r[0-9]+s[0-9]+)?$\"},\n    \"title\":    {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 5},\n    \"category\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"enum\": [\"micro_opt\",\"structural\",\"extension\",\"predictor\",\"memory\"]},\n    \"motivation\":  {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 20},\n    \"hypothesis\":  {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 20},\n    \"expected_impact\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\",\n      \"required\": [\"fitness_delta_pct\",\"confidence\"],\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"fitness_delta_pct\": {\"type\": \"integer\"},\n        \"confidence\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"enum\": [\"low\",\"medium\",\"high\"]}\n      }\n    },\n    \"changes\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\", \"minItems\": 1,\n      \"items\": {\n        \"type\": \"object\",\n        \"required\": [\"file\",\"description\"],\n        \"properties\": {\n          \"file\":        {\n            \"type\": \"string\",\n            \"description\": \"Must be under rtl/ (any extension) or be a test/test_*.py cocotb suite. Anything else is rejected by the runtime sandbox check.\",\n            \"pattern\": \"^(rtl/[^.].*|test/test_[^/]+\\\\.py)$\"\n          },\n          \"description\": {\"type\": \"string\"}\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_6", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg -n 'predictor|prediction|hyp-20261001-003-r[23]s2' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\"", "aggregated_output": "2:{\"id\": \"hyp-20261001-001-r1s0\", \"title\": \"Shared combinational radix-4 division with parallel trial subtracts\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"The only recorded experiment is the baseline; no LESSONS.md exists and\\nthere are no earlier micro_opt attempts to repeat. The baseline reports\\n5.442 MHz and an approximately 200 ns, 156-cell worst path through\\nforwarding and the combinational ALU. The ALU expresses signed and\\nunsigned division and remainder with separate / and % operators. These\\nare the strongest candidates for the deep arithmetic path, even when\\nCoreMark is executing an ordinary integer operation. Shortening this\\narithmetic network can raise Fmax without reducing iterations per cycle.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The only recorded experiment is the baseline; no LESSONS.md exists and\\nthere are no earlier micro_opt attempts to repeat. The baseline reports\\n5.442 MHz and an approximately 200 ns, 156-cell worst path through\\nforwarding and the combinational ALU. The ALU expresses signed and\\nunsigned division and remainder with separate / and % operators. These\\nare the strongest candidates for the deep arithmetic path, even when\\nCoreMark is executing an ordinary integer operation. Shortening this\\narithmetic network can raise Fmax without reducing iterations per cycle.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Replace only the real DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU datapath with one combinational\\nunsigned radix-4 restoring divider, shared by all four operations. Keep\\nthe ALU interface, execution latency, pipeline, forwarding, bus-stall\\nbehavior, and nret=1 port contract unchanged. Convert signed operands\\nto unsigned 32-bit magnitudes before the divider and correct quotient\\nand remainder signs afterward; unsigned operations use operands directly.\\n\\nUnroll 16 stages, each consuming two dividend bits. Precompute D, 2D,\\nand 3D once as 34-bit unsigned values. Each stage forms T=4*R+next_two_bits and\\ncomputes T-D, T-2D, and T-3D in parallel. Derive the three fit predicates\\nfrom the extended subtract results' borrow bit\n…[50201 of 53273 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:7629b76bbba4f2e9]…\nties.\\n\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Include the predictor alongside the champion divider in the source\\nlist and extend architectural prediction/recovery tests under bus,\\nload-use, and divider stalls without weakening existing checks.\\n\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 103.09, \"delta_pct\": 5.16, \"vs_baseline\": 750.58, \"fmax_mhz\": 43.316, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4201740, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 3252, \"ff\": 787, \"seeds\": [41.857, 43.316, 43.316], \"perturbations\": [[0, 41.857, 25], [1, 43.316, 25], [2, 43.316, 25]], \"lutram\": 8, \"bsram\": 6, \"dsp\": 6, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_rf/regs_regs_0_0_s0\", \"to\": \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu/u_divider/remainder_q_3_s1\", \"slack_ns\": -18.891, \"arrival_ns\": 29.185, \"logic_cells\": 25, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_id\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu/u_divider\"]}, \"logic_levels\": 25, \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-01T14:32:34.440057Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 3}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
