{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_5", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/LESSONS.md schemas/hypothesis.schema.json'", "aggregated_output": "- 2026-10-01 hyp-20261001-001-r1s0 (regression, +4.37%): Sharing DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU in a tapered radix-4 divider reduced logic cells by 60%, but parallel trial-subtract selection and routing kept division on the forwarding-to-ALU critical path, limiting Fmax improvement to 4.37% with unchanged CoreMark cycles.\n- 2026-10-01 hyp-20261001-002-r1s1 (improvement, +522.03%): A shared eight-edge divider with four restoring steps per clock breaks the combinational / and % chain feeding the EX result mux, making the Fmax gain outweigh blocking DIV/REM latency in CoreMark.\n- 2026-10-01 hyp-20261001-002-r2s1 (improvement, +30.03%): Separating a four-bit launch prefix with high-divisor guards from two radix-4 stages fed by registered D/3D multiples improves divider timing by removing live-operand muxing and halving serial full-width subtract/select decisions while retaining eight-edge latency.\n- 2026-10-01 hyp-20261001-003-r2s2 (regression, +16.21%): A 64-entry direction table with decoded B/J targets cuts stalled CoreMark cycles by 6.45%, but the register-file-to-divider launch path remains critical, so its throughput gain trails retiming that path.\n- 2026-10-01 hyp-20261001-001-r3s0 (regression, +6.69%): Combining forwarding and PC/immediate selection in parallel one-hot masked-OR muxes removes serial operand selection and improves Fmax with unchanged CoreMark cycles, shifting the critical path to divider launch.\n- 2026-10-01 hyp-20261001-002-r3s1 (improvement, +10.05%): Combining explicit flip-flop RF storage with validity-only ID/EX squash removes both BSRAM read-output absorption and redirect feedback through RF addresses and operand capture, improving Fmax with unchanged stalled CoreMark cycles.\n- 2026-10-01 hyp-20261001-001-r4s0 (regression, +11.57%): Boolean nibble quotient/remainder equations plus direct raw-operand normalization remove four dependent launch subtract/select stages and full-width magnitude dependencies, shifting the timing bottleneck to forwarding/ALU-to-memory with unchanged CoreMark cycles.\n- 2026-10-01 hyp-20261001-002-r4s1 (regression, +9.93%): A normalization-only launch followed by an eight-bit prefix stage breaks the forwarding-to-divider arithmetic chain while preserving eight-edge latency and CoreMark cycles, but the 256-entry case table infers an extra Gowin BSRAM and forwarding/multiplication-to-dmem becomes the timing limit.\n- 2026-10-01 hyp-20261001-003-r4s2 (improvement, +12.46%): Stateless backward-taken/JAL prediction exploits CoreMark loop locality, and matching IF/EX direct targets enables one-bit recovery that removes taken-control squash bubbles while avoiding the Fmax cost of direction-table lookup/update logic.\n{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"required\": [\"id\",\"title\",\"category\",\"motivation\",\"hypothesis\",\"expected_impact\",\"changes\"],\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"id\":       {\"type\": \"string\", \"pattern\": \"^hyp-[0-9]{8}-[0-9]{3}(-r[0-9]+s[0-9]+)?$\"},\n    \"title\":    {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 5},\n    \"category\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"enum\": [\"micro_opt\",\"structural\",\"extension\",\"predictor\",\"memory\"]},\n    \"motivation\":  {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 20},\n    \"hypothesis\":  {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 20},\n    \"expected_impact\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\",\n      \"required\": [\"fitness_delta_pct\",\"confidence\"],\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"fitness_delta_pct\": {\"type\": \"integer\"},\n        \"confidence\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"enum\": [\"low\",\"medium\",\"high\"]}\n      }\n    },\n    \"changes\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\", \"minItems\": 1,\n      \"items\": {\n        \"type\": \"object\",\n        \"required\": [\"file\",\"description\