1:5] tag, and hold a valid bit and\\ntwo-bit confidence counter per entry. A cache miss keeps backward-taken /\\nforward-not-taken prediction. A matching entry predicts the opposite of\\nthe instruction's static direction only while confidence has its high\\nbit set. Tags are performance metadata; instruction predecode and\\nalignment checks remain mandatory before any prediction is enabled.\\n\\nTrain confidence on whether the resolved direction differs from the\\ninstruction's static direction. Increment with saturation for an\\nexception and decrement with saturation for agre\n…[9807 of 12879 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:f76d635359684cfb]…\nacity exists, and atomically flush both entries on accepted correction.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\",\n      \"description\": \"Wire the current predictor to bus PC/data and feed hazard imem availability from the selected head validity rather than raw bus readiness; preserve every top-level port and existing EX/MEM/WB datapath.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\",\n      \"description\": \"Retain all architectural assertions; distinguish buffered decode PC from bus lookahead PC in two implementation-specific observations. Add occupancy/acceptance, empty/one/two-entry transitions, simultaneous pop/refill, full-queue corrections, overlapping waits, reset and wrong-path side-effect checks with contiguous RVFI order.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n\nhyp-20261001-003-r7s2 Four-entry predictor-directed fetch lookahead {'fitness': 161.29, 'fmax_mhz': 66.311, 'cycles': 4111263}\nhyp-20261001-003-r8s2 Prediction-guided fetch queue with validity-only recovery {'fitness': 179.84, 'fmax_mhz': 73.936, 'cycles': 4111263}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
