{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_62", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261001-003-r9s2.yaml');d=yaml.safe_load(p.read_text())\nd['title']='Static-agreement prediction trained from registered branch results'\nd['hypothesis']='''Extend the current direct-control predictor with one sixteen-entry static-\nagreement table indexed by PC[5:2]. Each two-bit saturating counter records\nagreement with BTFNT: reset to 3, increment when actual direction matches\ninstruction bit 31, and decrement on disagreement. For a legal aligned\nconditional branch predict instr[31] XOR \"'!counter[1]. Retain aligned JAL\nalways taken and JALR sequential. Preserve the existing 30-bit B/J target\naddition and legality/alignment guards. Aliases affect accuracy only because\ndirect targets always come from the actual fetched instruction.\n\nUse sixteen fixed two-bit flip-flop words with independent decoded enables;\nreset the 32 bits to strong agreement. No tags, valid bitmap, target storage,\nhistory, pending-event queue or RAM is required. Read only disagreement from\nthe counter MSBs, with constant-index address selects and a balanced OR tree.\nFor old high/low counter bits h,l and registered agreement a, implement exact\nsaturating next state as h_next=(h&l)|(a&(h|l)) and\nl_next=(h&~l)|(a&(h|~l)). Each next bit is a three-input Boolean function,\navoiding general add/subtract and saturation selection networks.\n\nTrain directly from the existing registered EX/MEM branch metadata, rather\nthan adding live EX resolution inputs or another update register. At its\noutgoing MEM acceptance edge, use ex_mem_w.pc for the update index and\nex_mem_w.branch_taken == ex_mem_w.instr[31] for agreement. Update once when\nex_mem_w.valid && !reset && !hold_mem_wb && ex_mem_w.ctrl.is_branch &&\n!ex_mem_w.ctrl.is_illegal && ex_mem_w.pc[1:0]==0 && !ex_mem_w.instr[8].\nThe branch has already survived EX validity, trap and downstream hold checks;\nthese register outputs isolate predictor feedback from live forwarded branch\noperands. Do not introduce an EX arithmetic or comparison operation for\ntraining. A held EX branch generates no repeated table updates, reset cancels\nupdates, and adjacent accepted branches update in order even at the same\nindex. Exclude misaligned direct targets conservatively even when not taken.\n\nPreserve the exact prediction already captured with every accepted fetch in\nthe queue and ID/EX. EX compares that captured bit with resolved effective\ndirection; never reconstruct it from the current counter. Retain one-bit\ncorrection and its priority, occupancy-only queue recovery, all payload\nlayouts, raw instruction paths, held forwarding data, registered MUL/DIV and\nALTOPS, default-illegal decode, alignment traps, resolved RVFI next PC,\ncontiguous retirement and exact-once memory effects. Keep nret=1 and all ports.\n\nRetain exhaustive B/J target, reserved-encoding and alignment assertions. Add\nan independent saturating-state model checking the Boolean equations, cold\nbias, both static directions, saturation, opposite-bias aliases, adjacent\nregistered updates and reset. Pipeline tests must combine queued predictions\nwith changed counters, loop exits, forward branches and every load/M/bus hold,\nchecking full architectural PC/RVFI/order/operand and wrong-path-store behavior.\nRun unchanged lint, formal/cosim and canonical CRC/UART/OOB/marker validation,\nand score all three Gowin placement options. No benchmark or correctness\ncontract changes are proposed. The acceptance threshold is 188.113 iter/sec;\nthe cycle savings must survive the FPGA timing cost of predictor state.\n'\"'''\nd['changes']=[\n {'file':'rtl/branch_predictor.sv','description':'Add sixteen fixed static-agreement counters, exact three-input Boolean saturating transitions, balanced one-bit read and strong-static reset. Accept updates directly from registered branch metadata; preserve legal/aligned direct prediction and exact B/J targets. Infer no RAM.'},\n {'file':'rtl/core.sv','description':'Wire predictor clock/reset and one accepted update from existing EX/MEM pc, instruction, branch_taken, validity and post-trap controls. Preserve EX logic, every top-level port, retirement width, fetch queue and all other datapaths.'},\n {'file':'test/test_branch_predictor.py','description':'Retain exhaustive direct target, legality and alignment assertions; add independent arithmetic counter references for Boolean transitions, bias, saturation, opposite-bias aliases, adjacent registered events and reset.'},\n {'file':'test/test_pipeline.py','description':'Preserve architectural assertions; cover queued predictions while counters change and branch training/correction during each hold reason, exact-once effects and complete RVFI PC/order/operand checks.'}]\np.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(d,sort_keys=False,width=95));jsonschema.validate(d,json.load(open('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json')))\nprint('Updated schema-valid proposal with registered EX/MEM training')\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
