{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_67","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261001-003-r9s2.yaml');d=yaml.safe_load(p.read_text());d['title']='Hashed static-agreement prediction from registered branch results'\nd['hypothesis']=d['hypothesis'].replace('sixteen-entry','32-entry').replace('PC[5:2]','PC[6:2] XOR PC[11:7]').replace('sixteen fixed','32 fixed').replace('reset the 32 bits','reset the 64 bits');d['changes'][0]['description']=d['changes'][0]['description'].replace('sixteen fixed','32 fixed')\nd['motivation']='''The champion uses backward-taken/forward-not-taken direction prediction and a\nfour-entry prediction-guided queue. Previous bimodal and tagged exception\npredictors reduced cycles but lost FPGA timing. An agreement predictor learns\nwhether to keep or invert each instruction's own static bias, so oppositely\nbiased branches can share counters constructively. A small PC-folded table\nneeds no tags, target RAM, valid bitmap or speculative history.\n\nAn isolated 32-entry prototype with PC[6:2] XOR PC[11:7] indexing, fixed FF\ncounters, Boolean saturating transitions and training from registered EX/MEM\nmetadata measured 4,030,475 canonical marked cycles versus 4,111,263 for the\nchampion, a 2.004 percent throughput gain. Gowin placement options measured\n75.164, 73.966 and 73.966 MHz: median 73.966 MHz and fitness 183.517 iter/sec,\na 2.045 percent gain over 179.84. It passed lint, all canonical CRC/UART/OOB/\nmarker checks and eight complete selftest/random RVFI trace comparisons with\nand without bus stalls. The counter transition truth table matches independent\nsaturating integer arithmetic for every state and both outcomes. Formal and\nfull cocotb gates remain for implementation; arithmetic was untouched.\n\nThese prototype results do not yet meet the 4.6 percent acceptance margin.\nAt the measured cycles qualification requires median Fmax above 75.817 MHz.\nThe single proposed mechanism is compact static-agreement prediction; its\nremaining risk is physical routing and the cost of lookup/update state.\n'''\nd['expected_impact']={'fitness_delta_pct':2,'confidence':'low'}\np.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(d,sort_keys=False,width=95));jsonschema.validate(d,json.load(open('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json')));print('Saved validated 32-entry hypothesis with measured evidence and acceptance limitation')\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
