{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_9", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor line in open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'):\n x=json.loads(line)\n if x['id'].endswith(('r3s1','r12s0','r11s2')):\n  print(x['id'])\n  print(x.get('hypothesis',{}).get('hypothesis',''))\n  print(x.get('implementation_notes',''))\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20261001-002-r3s1\nRestructure the existing fetch/decode-to-execute operand boundary so\nwide instruction/operand payload is stored independently of instruction\nvalidity, and integer register reads terminate in actual ID/EX operand\nflip-flops. These are complementary requirements of the same boundary:\nthe array-style RF permits Gowin BSRAM read-output absorption, while\nredirect-to-NOP masking feeds branch resolution back into read addresses\nand wide ID/EX update logic. Preserve stage count, the single-issue\npipeline, sequential branch policy, and the current eight-edge divider.\n\nReplace the RF array with 31 individually generated 32-bit flip-flop\nwords, each having its own synchronous reset and decoded write enable;\nx0 is constant zero. Organize the read network as four groups of eight\nregister numbers. For each of two independent ports, share a five-bit\none-hot address decoder, mask words with their selects, reduce each\neight-word group with balanced OR logic, then combine the four groups.\nUse fixed-index wiring rather than dynamic array accesses, so storage\ncannot be inferred as RAM. Both ports must read arbitrary register pairs\nwithout bank conflicts. Preserve write-first bypass on both ports and\nx0 priority. Do not add registers inside reg_file or change port latency.\n\nExpose raw imem_data and PC to decode, RF addresses and load-use matching\nwithout the current redirect/flush NOP mux. Fetch validity is imemReady,\nindependent of redirect. Set hold = dmem_stall || divider_wait and\nkill = load_use || accepted_redirect. On every nonheld edge, capture the\nraw decoded payload and operands into ID/EX, regardless of kill or fetch\nreadiness; separately set valid = fetch_valid && !kill. Reset initializes\npayload and clears valid. A true hold retains both. Load-use holds PC,\nlets the load advance, and creates exactly one invalid EX slot; admit\nthe still-fetched dependent on the next available edge. Redirect kills\nthe younger slot and updates PC with existing priority over imem stalls.\nAn older unaccepted memory reques\n…[12303 of 15375 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:3b0a5dd26af0e13d]…\nsis must confirm\nFF storage and the final selection order rather than assume them.\n\nExtend RF tests to exercise all four addresses, concurrent same-address\nreads, independent write-first matches, x0 and reset. Extend pipeline\nchecks with the architectural identity selected_operand == RF(selected\ninstruction source), including distinct live/head instructions, WB\nmatches on only one source, empty/full queues, pop/refill, instruction\nand data stalls, load/M replay, direct recovery and ready/unready JALR\nlandings. Retain every existing assertion and cycle deadline. Run lint,\nthe existing unit suite, unchanged single-retire formal gate, full-trace\nstalled/unstalled cosim and canonical marked CoreMark with CRC/UART/bounds\nchecks. Expect the same 4,052,037 marked cycles. At unchanged cycles the\n4.6-percent acceptance margin needs median Gowin Fmax above approximately\n91.75 MHz; measure all three placement options. The proposed eight-percent\nimprovement is an unmeasured timing estimate, not a completed experiment.\n\n\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
