{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_43", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261002-001-r13s0.yaml'", "aggregated_output": "id: hyp-20261002-001-r13s0\ntitle: \"LUT-native binary mux trees for flip-flop register reads\"\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  The champion scores 216.47 iter/sec at 87.715 MHz with 4,052,037\n  marker-bracketed CoreMark cycles. Its reported worst path starts at\n  fetch-queue count_q and ends at ID/EX rs2_val through the register file:\n  16.717 ns and ten logic cells. The RF currently decodes full one-hot\n  source addresses, masks 32 words, reduces them through OR trees, then\n  applies x0 and write-first bypass. This is a substantial combinational\n  cone after fetch-source selection. The r12s0/r12s2 duplicate-read\n  attempts added about 1,440 LUTs and regressed timing; r12s1 source\n  sidecars added capture-enable fanout and also regressed. A local RF\n  read-network rewrite avoids those demonstrated area and queue costs.\nhypothesis: |\n  Replace only the two combinational masked-OR RF read networks with\n  explicit, balanced, fixed-index binary mux trees. Keep the existing\n  31 individually generated 32-bit writable flip-flop words, constant\n  x0 word, independent synchronous reset and decoded write enables.\n  For each read port independently, pair fixed adjacent words using\n  source address bit 0, pair those outputs using bit 1, then bits 2,\n  3 and 4, forming a complete five-level 32-to-1 tree. Every leaf and\n  intermediate connection has a constant elaboration index; do not\n  replace this with variable-index array reads that could infer RAM.\n  Express each node as a plain two-way conditional mux so Gowin can\n  pack compatible levels into its LUT4 and dedicated mux resources.\n  Do not add preservation attributes that prevent this packing.\n\n  Remove the read-only one-hot decoders, full-address word masks and\n  OR reductions. Keep the write decoder and storage behavior exactly\n  equivalent. Preserve both ports' combinational write-first bypass,\n  with x0 having priority even when w_en writes address zero. The\n  public reg_file interface and its zero-cycle read latency stay the\n  same. Both ports must read every pai\n…[1679 of 4751 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:7795a15a7b61096d]…\nsses and exactly 4,052,037 marked cycles.\n  Measure all three vendor Gowin placements, verify zero RF BSRAMs and\n  unchanged writable storage, and inspect whether the occupancy-to-RF\n  critical path actually shrinks rather than merely moving placement.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 8\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/reg_file.sv\n    description: |\n      Replace the two fixed-index one-hot masked-OR read networks with\n      five-level fixed-index binary mux trees suitable for Gowin LUT\n      and dedicated mux packing. Preserve the existing FF word storage,\n      write decoder, interface, synchronous reset, x0 and write-first\n      bypass with no additional latency or read ports.\n  - file: test/test_reg_file.py\n    description: |\n      Retain all independent architectural-array checks and existing\n      assertions. Extend directed coverage of address-bit boundaries\n      during simultaneous writes and independent source transitions,\n      including x0, either/both-port bypass and reset priority.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
