{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_39", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\nfrom pathlib import Path\nf=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261002-001-r14s0.yaml')\nd=yaml.safe_load(f.read_text())\nd['title']='Compute branch predicates before forwarding operand selection'\nd['motivation']='''The champion reaches 216.47 iterations/sec at 87.715 MHz with 4,052,037\nmarked CoreMark cycles. Recent operand-delivery changes repeatedly expose\nforwarded-operand-to-fetch-recovery paths. r13s0 changed only the branch\ncomparator topology and regressed by 1.84 percent. An isolated complete\none-hot operand-mask probe also missed qualification at 86.797 MHz,\nwith unchanged cycles and a 36-cell branch-recovery path. Instead of\nchanging the carry chain or adding stages, commute branch comparison\nbefore the two forwarding data muxes, so bypass control selects only\none-bit comparison results.'''\nd['hypothesis']='''Change only the EX branch-condition datapath. Independently compare\nall three available architectural rs1 sources (ID/EX.rs1_val,\nEX/MEM.alu_result, and the authoritative retained MEM/WB result) with\nall three rs2 sources (ID/EX.rs2_val and those same two bypass words).\nCreate fixed-index 3-by-3 banks of equality and unsigned-less predicates\nbefore forwarding selection. Use ordinary native == and < expressions\nso Gowin retains its efficient carry mapping; do not substitute a new\ncarry-select arithmetic network or the unsuccessful r13s0 comparator.\nComparisons of a bypass word with itself are constant equal/never-less.\nThe EX/MEM versus MEM/WB comparison is shared with its reversed pair:\nreverse less is \"'!equal && !less. Synthesis may naturally deduplicate\nthese predicates; preserve exact values for all other pairs.\n\nDecode the existing registered two-bit forwarding selectors into three\nexclusive enables, preserving 00/default=RF, 01=EX/MEM and 10=MEM/WB.\nFirst select each row'\"'s one-bit equality and less predicates using rs2\nenables, then select among the three rows using rs1 enables. Use small\nfixed masked-OR reductions. A forwarding selector must never precede a\nwide branch comparator's operand input; only one-bit predicate selection\nfollows the comparators. Derive signed less after predicate selection\nwith the existing forwarded sign bits: signs differ ? rs1[31] : unsigned\nless. Keep explicit BEQ/BNE/BLT/BGE/BLTU/BGEU case selection and reserved\ncase false. No extra stage, register, direction predictor, or latency\nis introduced. This is a single speculation/selection micro-optimization\nof the branch comparison network, not a change to producer eligibility.\n\nKeep the ordinary forwarded rs1/rs2 data muxes for every other consumer:\nALU, effective_addr, JALR, store data, MEM multiply operands and raw RVFI\nmetadata. Retained MEM/WB data must remain available even when WB.valid\nis cleared on a memory hold. Both branch predicate banks and ordinary\nfunctional operands use exactly those same three source words and the\nsame registered forwarding selectors. Preserve younger-writer priority,\nx0 behavior, actual and ALTOPS arithmetic, eight-edge divider launch,\nsticky completion and source capture, multiply replay, load-use rules,\nfour-entry fetch queue, static prediction, direct recovery PC preselection\nand registered JALR landing. Preserve every trap/alignment gate and\ncontrol-acceptance condition, nret=1, all top-level ports, default-illegal\ndecoding, contiguous in-order retirement and exact-once memory effects.\n\nTest against independent Python signed/unsigned/equality references\nfor all nine forwarding combinations, both operands selecting the same\nbypass word, simultaneous matching producers, opposite signs, equality,\nzero and extrema, seeded random data, reversed EX/MEM versus MEM/WB,\nall six legal branches and both reserved branch_op values. Include\nmemory holds retaining WB, divider drain, predicted hits/misses,\nmisaligned and invalid/killed branches, raw source aliases and wrong-path\nmemory suppression. Retain every existing architectural and latency\nassertion. Run unchanged lint, single-retire formal and full RVFI cosim\nwith and without bus stalls. Require canonical CoreMark CRC/UART/bounds\nvalidation and exactly 4,052,037 marker-bracketed cycles. Measure all\nthree vendor placements; at unchanged cycles qualification needs over\n226.42762 iterations/sec, approximately 91.749 MHz median Fmax.\nThe duplicated predicates increase LUT count and source-word fanout;\nRF capture, divider prefix, base ALU or recovery routing may limit the\ngain. The estimated improvement is not a measured acceptance result.'''\nd['expected_impact']={'fitness_delta_pct':7,'confidence':'low'}\nd['changes']=[\n {'file':'rtl/ex_stage.sv','description':'Move only branch equality and unsigned-less comparisons before forwarding data selection; use fixed 3-by-3 predicate banks and small one-bit row/column selection, with shared same-source and reversed-bypass cases. Preserve signed branch semantics, case defaults, ordinary operand muxes and every recovery/trap/acceptance rule.'},\n {'file':'test/test_ex_stage.py','description':'Retain all existing expectations and timing bounds; independently test all branch operations and nine bypass-source pairs across random and directed operands, same-source equality, reversed bypass words, sign boundaries, reserved encodings, invalid payloads and alignment.'},\n {'file':'test/test_pipeline.py','description':'Retain all retirement, memory, prediction and latency assertions; extend branch source association and youngest-writer priority across memory holds, divider drain, prediction hits/misses, forwarded operands, reset and wrong-path side effects.'}]\njsonschema.validate(d,json.load(open('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json')))\nf.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(d,sort_keys=False,width=78))\nprint('Updated schema-valid hypothesis',f)\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_39", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\nfrom pathlib import Path\nf=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261002-001-r14s0.yaml')\nd=yaml.safe_load(f.read_text())\nd['title']='Compute branch predicates before forwarding operand selection'\nd['motivation']='''The champion reaches 216.47 iterations/sec at 87.715 MHz with 4,052,037\nmarked CoreMark cycles. Recent operand-delivery changes repeatedly expose\nforwarded-operand-to-fetch-recovery paths. r13s0 changed only the branch\ncomparator topology and regressed by 1.84 percent. An isolated complete\none-hot operand-mask probe also missed qualification at 86.797 MHz,\nwith unchanged cycles and a 36-cell branch-recovery path. Instead of\nchanging the carry chain or adding stages, commute branch comparison\nbefore the two forwarding data muxes, so bypass control selects only\none-bit comparison results.'''\nd['hypothesis']='''Change only the EX branch-condition datapath. Independently compare\nall three available architectural rs1 sources (ID/EX.rs1_val,\nEX/MEM.alu_result, and the authoritative retained MEM/WB result) with\nall three rs2 sources (ID/EX.rs2_val and those same two bypass words).\nCreate fixed-index 3-by-3 banks of equality and unsigned-less predicates\nbefore forwarding selection. Use ordinary native == and < expressions\nso Gowin retains its efficient carry mapping; do not substitute a new\ncarry-select arithmetic network or the unsuccessful r13s0 comparator.\nComparisons of a bypass word with itself are constant equal/never-less.\nThe EX/MEM versus MEM/WB comparison is shared with its reversed pair:\nreverse less is \"'!equal && !less. Synthesis may naturally deduplicate\nthese predicates; preserve exact values for all other pairs.\n\nDecode the existing registered two-bit forwarding selectors into three\nexclusive enables, preserving 00/default=RF, 01=EX/MEM and 10=MEM/WB.\nFirst select each row'\"'s one-bit equality and less predicates using rs2\nenables, then select among the three rows using rs1 enables. Use small\nfixed masked-OR reductions. A forwarding selector must never precede a\nwide branch comparator's operand input; only one-bit predicate selection\nfollows the comparators. Derive signed less after predicate selection\nwith the existing forwarded sign bits: signs differ ? rs1[31] : unsigned\nless. Keep explicit BEQ/BNE/BLT/BGE/BLTU/BGEU case selection and reserved\ncase false. No extra stage, register, direction predictor, or latency\nis introduced. This is a single speculation/selection micro-optimization\nof the branch comparison network, not a change to producer eligibility.\n\nKeep the ordinary forwarded rs1/rs2 data muxes for every other consumer:\nALU, effective_addr, JALR, store data, MEM multiply operands and raw RVFI\nmetadata. Retained MEM/WB data must remain available even when WB.valid\nis cleared on a memory hold. Both branch predicate banks and ordinary\nfunctional operands use exactly those same three source words and the\nsame registered forwarding selectors. Preserve younger-writer priority,\nx0 behavior, actual and ALTOPS arithmetic, eight-edge divider launch,\nsticky completion and source capture, multiply replay, load-use rules,\nfour-entry fetch queue, static prediction, direct recovery PC preselection\nand registered JALR landing. Preserve every trap/alignment gate and\ncontrol-acceptance condition, nret=1, all top-level ports, default-illegal\ndecoding, contiguous in-order retirement and exact-once memory effects.\n\nTest against independent Python signed/unsigned/equality references\nfor all nine forwarding combinations, both operands selecting the same\nbypass word, simultaneous matching producers, opposite signs, equality,\nzero and extrema, seeded random data, reversed EX/MEM versus MEM/WB,\nall six legal branches and both reserved branch_op values. Include\nmemory holds retaining WB, divider drain, pre