{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_62", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\nfrom pathlib import Path\nf=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261002-001-r14s0.yaml')\nd=yaml.safe_load(f.read_text())\nd['title']='Precompute direct-recovery decisions for both branch outcomes'\nd['motivation']='''The champion scores 216.47 iterations/sec at 87.715 MHz and\n4,052,037 marked CoreMark cycles. Recent RF and branch-comparison probes\nrepeatedly expose EX branch-condition-to-fetch-recovery paths. r13s0's\nbalanced comparator regressed, and isolated predicate replication also\nincreased routing delay. r11s2's winning direct-target preselection\nshows that moving instruction-dependent recovery work before ID/EX can\nimprove Fmax without adding bubbles. Apply that principle to the direct\nredirect decision itself, using only two small metadata bits.'''\nd['hypothesis']='''Precompute the direct-redirect truth table for both possible branch\ncomparison outcomes before the existing ID/EX edge. Keep branch\ncomparisons, forwarding data muxes and every arithmetic datapath exactly\nas the champion implements them. In ID, reuse the existing current\nvalidated decoder controls and direct_target_pc = in.pc + imm.\nDefine B = dec_is_branch && \"'!dec_is_illegal &&\n           (direct_target_pc[1:0] == 0), and\nJ = dec_is_jump && !dec_is_jalr && !dec_is_illegal &&\n    (direct_target_pc[1:0] == 0).\nRegister R0 = in.predicted_taken XOR J and\nR1 = in.predicted_taken XOR (J OR B). These are respectively the direct\ncorrection requests for branch_cond=0 and branch_cond=1.\n\nPlace the two bits in a sideband register owned by id_stage, with the\nsame synchronous reset and true downstream hold as the ID/EX payload.\nReset both bits to zero. Capture them on every non-held payload edge,\nincluding killed slots and missing fetch responses; those affect only\nID/EX.valid. Expose the two-bit sideband to EX through core wiring, so\nexisting packed payload positions and raw RVFI metadata remain intact.\nThis adds two metadata flip-flops and no instruction/data stage.\n\nReplace only EX'\"'s direct direction-mismatch expression with\ncontrol_accept && (branch_cond ? R1 : R0).\nKeep control_accept exactly in.valid && \"'!reset && !stall && !divider_wait.\nFor cond=false, direct_taken is J; for cond=true it is J OR B, so this\nis exactly the existing (direct_taken XOR predicted_taken) for legal,\nillegal, aligned and misaligned direct control flow. JAL and ordinary\ninstructions have R0=R1. The late branch data path now selects between\nalready-qualified one-bit correction requests instead of traversing\nis_branch/is_jump/is_jalr, alignment, legality and prediction XOR logic\nbefore the fetch recovery network. Perform those qualifications before\nthe register, not by rebuilding B/J from live EX controls.\n\nKeep the existing branch_cond case and signed/unsigned/equality\ncomparators; do not use duplicated branch predicates or a replacement\ncarry network. Preserve misalign_branch, misalign_direct,\nmisalign_indirect, ctrl_with_trap and next_w_en separately and exactly,\nincluding branch traps and suppressed JAL/JALR link writes. Keep\nredirect = direct_redirect OR indirect_accept, the existing direct\nrecovery target, immediate JALR squash and registered indirect landing.\nThis proposal changes neither direction prediction nor recovery latency.\nKeep the fetch queue, bus acceptance, ready/unready landing behavior,\nload-use and multiply replay, authoritative retained WB forwarding,\nactual and ALTOPS M arithmetic, divider source capture, eight-edge\ncompletion and sticky consume behavior. Preserve nret=1, all top-level\nports, decoder default-illegal discipline, every alignment/trap check,\ncontiguous retirement and exact-once memory effects. An unused original\nprediction field may remain for bundle compatibility; suppress only its\nlocal lint warning rather than changing offsets or weakening checks.\n\nValidate the two-bit sideband'\"'s association with the actual ID/EX slot\nthrough reset, kill, empty fetch, queue consumption, load/M replay,\nprolonged dmem/divider holds, branch correction and indirect landing.\nIndependently compare direct_redirect with the original qualified\nprediction-mismatch expression for both outcomes, all legal branch\nkinds, JAL/JALR, ordinary and illegal instructions, target low-bit\npatterns, forward/backward predictions and wrapping PCs. Keep every\nexisting architectural and latency assertion, including misaligned\nbranch/jump trap and wrong-path memory suppression. Run unchanged lint,\nID/EX/pipeline tests, all single-retire ALTOPS formal checks and full\nRVFI cosim with and without bus stalls. Require canonical CoreMark\nCRCs, UART validation, bounded memory, markers and exactly 4,052,037\nmarked cycles; measure all three vendor placements. Acceptance at\nunchanged cycles requires over 226.42762 iterations/sec, approximately\n91.749 MHz median Fmax. RF capture, divider prefix and the retained\nbranch comparator remain competing limits; the estimated gain requires\nvendor confirmation.'''\nd['expected_impact']={'fitness_delta_pct':6,'confidence':'low'}\nd['changes']=[\n {'file':'rtl/id_stage.sv','description':'Compute aligned legal direct-branch/direct-jump eligibility with current decode and target low bits; capture two prediction-mismatch outcome bits in sideband FFs with exactly the ID/EX reset, hold and validity-only squash schedule.'},\n {'file':'rtl/ex_stage.sv','description':'Replace only direct direction-mismatch qualification with selection of the registered false/true outcome bits by the unchanged branch_cond. Keep branch comparison, control acceptance, trap suppression, forwarding, targets and indirect recovery unchanged.'},\n {'file':'rtl/core.sv','description':'Wire the two-bit direct-recovery sideband from ID to EX without changing top-level IO, packed payload layout, pipeline stage count or RVFI behavior.'},\n {'file':'test/test_id_stage.py','description':'Retain all payload and validity assertions; verify outcome-bit capture, reset and hold with independent decode/target expectations, including kills, unavailable fetch responses, alignment and wrapping PCs.'},\n {'file':'test/test_ex_stage.py','description':'Adapt direct-stage stimulus to provide the new sideband for its instruction; retain every expected result and timing bound. Compare the selected request against the original qualified mismatch across both outcomes and all instruction/control/alignment classes.'},\n {'file':'test/test_pipeline.py','description':'Retain every architectural and latency assertion; verify sideband/payload association through queued fetch, load/M replay, memory/divider holds, prediction hits/misses, direct corrections, JALR landing, misalignment and wrong-path effects.'}]\njsonschema.validate(d,json.load(open('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json')))\nf.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(d,sort_keys=False,width=78))\nprint('Updated schema-valid hypothesis',f)\n# Prediction is no longer functionally used by EX; preserve packed layout.\np=Path('/srv/hwebench/tmp/555e5898/378d9cd2/r14-recovery/cores/bench/rtl/ex_stage.sv')\ns=p.read_text().replace('  input  id_ex_t   in,','  /* verilator lint_off UNUSEDSIGNAL */\\\\n  input  id_ex_t   in,\\\\n  /* verilator lint_on UNUSEDSIGNAL */');p.write_text(s)\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
