{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_73", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\nfrom pathlib import Path\nf=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261002-001-r14s0.yaml')\nd=yaml.safe_load(f.read_text())\nd['title']='Decode fetch-queue append destinations before the hazard decision'\nd['motivation']='''The champion scores 216.47 iterations/sec at 87.715 MHz with\n4,052,037 marked CoreMark cycles. r12s1 exposed a queue occupancy through\nsource hazard, hold and append path into a payload sidecar; other RF\nand branch changes also exposed queue-control timing. Isolated smaller\noperand/recovery probes in this turn passed functional checks but missed\nqualification, with fetch-queue payload writes again limiting timing.\nThe existing append destination subtracts the late pop decision from\nthree-bit count and then decodes it, placing arithmetic and destination\nselection after decode hazard logic. Factor that exact Boolean function\ninto constant per-bank occupancy predicates before the late stall bit.'''\nd['hypothesis']='''Make one local combinational control optimization in if_stage; keep\nthe four-entry queue, binary occupancy register, payload banks, empty\nfallthrough, prediction and every acquisition/recovery rule unchanged.\nReplace append_index = count_q - (storage_pop ? 1 : 0) and its case\nstatement with four fixed bank append enables. For bank k=0..3 use\nappend_enable[k] = imem_ready &&\n                  (((count_q == k) && stall) ||\n                   ((count_q == k+1) && \"'!stall)).\nUse explicitly sized three-bit constants and fixed-index generated wires.\nThese equalities are computed directly from registered occupancy, in\nparallel with the fetch/head selection and hazard path. The late stall\nbit chooses already-decoded candidate destinations, avoiding a three-bit\nsubtract and a subsequent variable append-index decoder.\n\nFor count=0, only a held decode enqueues the ready raw response in bank\n0; an unheld response falls through and writes no bank. For count=1..3,\na hold appends at bank count while a pop/refill appends at count-1. For\ncount=4, a hold writes no bank and a ready pop/refill writes bank3. With\nimem_ready=0 no bank appends, but an occupied unheld queue still shifts\nand drains. Retain the current shift assignments on storage_pop and\nlet each bank'\"'s append assignment override its shift, exactly as today.\nDo not put reset, redirect or validity gates on payload-bank writes;\noccupancy-only flush makes speculative writes unreachable.\n\nKeep storage_pop, storage_accept, storage_bypass and storage_enqueue\nsemantics for PC acquisition and occupancy updates. In particular PC\nmust advance only on the existing storage_accept, independent of decode\nconsumption, and count must update only on the same enqueue/pop pair.\nRetain storage_enqueue if needed for occupancy even though payload\nwrites now use direct bank predicates. Remove the unused append_index\nsignal and the arithmetic/case datapath entirely. Do not add sidecar\nstate, extra RF reads, a new FIFO representation or any instruction\nstage. This is Boolean factoring of existing queue destination control,\nnot a new memory architecture or predictor.\n\nKeep the raw response PC/prediction fields, full pop/refill behavior,\nappend-over-shift priority, no-wait empty bypass, direct recovery PC\npreselection, immediate indirect squash and registered JALR landing.\nReady landing responses predict their own successors; an unaccepted\nlanding commits its target before the bypass disappears. Preserve every\nload-use and multiply replay, true dmem/divider hold, retained WB bypass,\nactual/ALTOPS arithmetic, eight-edge division, default-illegal decoding,\ntrap/alignment gate, nret=1 port and RVFI contract, contiguous retirement,\nexact-once memory effect and every existing test/latency assertion.\n\nCheck the new per-bank enables against the original queue transaction\nsemantics for all legal occupancies 0..4, both stall values and both\nimem_ready values, and compare complete payload order with the existing\nindependent deque model. Cover append-only, pop-only, simultaneous\npop/refill at every occupied depth, full hold, empty bypass, prolonged\nbackpressure, live imem changes while unready, reset/redirect with\nspeculative writes and ready/unready indirect landing. Preserve content,\nPC, prediction and acquisition assertions, not just enable equivalence.\nRun unchanged lint, queue/pipeline unit tests, single-retire ALTOPS\nformal and full-RVFI cosim with and without bus stalls. Require canonical\nCoreMark CRC/UART/bounds/marker checks and exactly 4,052,037 marked\ncycles, then all three Gowin placements. Qualification at unchanged\ncycles requires over 226.42762 iterations/sec, approximately 91.749 MHz\nmedian Fmax. Predicate fanout, payload shift mux routing and competing\nRF/divider/branch paths can limit the gain; vendor timing must establish\nwhether this factoring removes enough delay to clear the margin.'''\nd['expected_impact']={'fitness_delta_pct':7,'confidence':'low'}\nd['changes']=[\n {'file':'rtl/if_stage.sv','description':'Replace subtract-and-case append destination logic with four fixed occupancy/stall/ready bank enables, preserving shift ordering and append priority. Keep every PC, count, bus acceptance, prediction, reset and recovery equation unchanged.'},\n {'file':'test/test_if_stage_queue.py','description':'Retain the independent deque and all payload/PC/prediction assertions. Exhaustively check append destinations for legal occupancies and all ready/stall combinations, and exercise full refill, empty bypass, unready data, holds, flush/reset and indirect landing.'},\n {'file':'test/test_pipeline.py','description':'Retain all architectural and latency checks; exercise queue refill/drain across load/M replay, dmem/divider holds, predicted flow, direct correction and JALR landing while checking exact-once ordered retirement and wrong-path memory suppression.'}]\njsonschema.validate(d,json.load(open('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json')))\nf.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(d,sort_keys=False,width=78))\nprint('Updated schema-valid hypothesis',f)\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
