n\nsemantics for all legal occupancies 0..4, both stall values and both\nimem_ready values, and compare complete payload order with the existing\nindependent deque model. Cover append-only, pop-only, simultaneous\npop/refill at every occupied depth, full hold, empty bypass, prolonged\nbackpressure, live imem changes while unready, reset/redirect with\nspeculative writes and ready/unready indirect landing. Preserve content,\nPC, prediction and acquisition assertions, not just enable equivalence.\nRun unchanged lint, queue/pipeline unit tests, single-retire ALTOPS\nformal and full-RVFI cosim with and without bus stalls. Require canonical\nCoreMark CRC/UART/bounds/marker checks and exactly 4,052,037 marked\ncycles, then all three Gowin placements. Qualification at unchanged\ncycles requires over 226.42762 iterations/sec, approximately 91.749 MHz\nmedian Fmax. Predicate fanout, payload shift mux routing and competing\nRF/divider/branch paths can limit the gain; vendor timing must establish\nwhether this factoring removes enough delay to clear the margin.'''\nd['expected_impact']={'fitness_delta_pct':7,'confidence':'low'}\nd['changes']=[\n {'file':'rtl/if_stage.sv','description':'Replace subtract-and-case append destination logic with four fixed occupancy/stall/ready bank enables, preserving shift ordering and append priority. Keep every PC, count, bus acceptance, prediction, reset and recovery equation unchanged.'},\n {'file':'test/test_if_stage_queue.py','description':'Retain the independent deque and all payload/PC/prediction assertions. Exhaustively check append destinations for legal occupancies and all ready/stall combinations, and exercise full refill, empty bypass, unready data, holds, flush/reset and indirect landing.'},\n {'file':'test/test_pipeline.py','description':'Retain all architectural and latency checks; exercise queue refill/drain across load/M replay, dmem/divider holds, predicted flow, direct correction and JALR landing while checking exact-once ordered retirement and wrong-path memory suppression.'}]\njsonschema.validate(d,json.load(open('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json')))\nf.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(d,sort_keys=False,width=78))\nprint('Updated schema-valid hypothesis',f)\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "Updated schema-valid hypothesis cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261002-001-r14s0.yaml\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
