{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"agent_message","text":"Recent attempts expose the forwarded base-ALU path as a competing timing limit. An earlier experiment gained 6.69% by combining forwarding and ALU operand selection, but the current RTL still uses those muxes in series. I’m focusing on that local optimization while preserving the pipeline and instruction latencies."}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor line in open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'):\n d=json.loads(line)\n if d['id']=='hyp-20261001-001-r3s0':\n  h=d['hypothesis']\n  print(h['hypothesis'])\n  print(d.get('implementation_notes'))\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_12", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor line in open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'):\n d=json.loads(line)\n if d['id']=='hyp-20261001-001-r3s0':\n  h=d['hypothesis']\n  print(h['hypothesis'])\n  print(d.get('implementation_notes'))\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "Replace encoded forwarding selects and cascaded data muxes with\nmutually exclusive one-hot source enables and parallel masked-OR\noperand selection. This is one local combinational mux optimization;\nkeep pipeline registers, divider latency, prediction, and bus handling.\n\nFor each EX source, compute M = EX/MEM valid writer, nonzero destination,\nand matching source register; W = MEM/WB ctrl.reg_write, nonzero destination,\nand matching source register. Emit three exclusive source enables:\nID = !M && !W, EXMEM = M, MEMWB = !M && W. Preserve EX/MEM priority and\nx0 behavior exactly. Preserve MEM/WB forwarding without valid qualification:\nits retained payload is required while dmem holds a dependent instruction.\nCarry these three enables directly into EX rather than encoding them\ninto two bits and decoding them again. Use [0]=ID, [1]=EXMEM and\n[2]=MEMWB, i.e. fwd_rs = {!M && W, M, !M && !W}. W must retain the\nexisting eligibility from ctrl.reg_write even when MEM/WB valid is clear.\n\nSelect architectural rs1 and rs2 with parallel masked ORs over ID/EX,\nEX/MEM, and MEM/WB data. For the ALU operands, qualify those source enables\nwith !is_auipc or !alu_src and add the mutually exclusive PC or immediate\nsource. Specifically form a_sel = {is_auipc, fwd_rs1 & {3{!is_auipc}}}\nand b_sel = {alu_src, fwd_rs2 & {3{!alu_src}}}. Construct ALU operands\nas ORs of four data words ANDed with their replicated source enable;\n[3] selects PC for A and immediate for B. Construct architectural rs1\nand rs2 as the analogous three-source masked ORs using unqualified\nforwarding enables. Select all four ALU candidates in parallel rather\nthan first constructing the forwarded operand and then applying a second\n32-bit PC/immediate mux. Branch comparisons, JALR and store data must\ncontinue to use architectural forwarded rs1/rs2, while AUIPC and immediate\nALU operations use the qualified ALU masks. Divider operand capture for\nRVFI must still report architectural sources, never substituted PC/imm.\n\nThe expected benefit is less serial select/decode and wid\n…[1804 of 4876 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:0b43d65491eb623c]…\nreturning through IF/hazard/ID.\n\nAll 18 existing pipeline cocotb cases passed. Full retirement-trace cosim\npassed selftest and all three random programs both with ready-high buses\nand with random instruction/data stalls, eight checks total. Canonical\nstalled CoreMark passed all five CRCs, the required UART validation\nliteral, bounded-access and termination checks. Its markers remained\n15,801 and 4,507,286, exactly 4,491,485 measured cycles for ten iterations.\nPrototype fitness is 103.10 iterations/second versus the champion's\n98.03. These are measurements of a temporary candidate implementation;\nthe orchestrator must still implement this proposal and run every gate.\nThe prototype changed only forward_unit.sv, ex_stage.sv and core.sv.\n\nAn isolated copy of the unchanged single-retire formal wrapper and\nchecks_si.cfg passed all 53 ALTOPS formal checks with zero failures.\nThis verifies operand routing and pipeline behavior; actual arithmetic\nwas exercised by the pipeline and retirement-trace simulations above.\n\n\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
