{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_44","type":"agent_message","text":"The predecode prototype also preserves CoreMark cycles, but its timing gain falls short. I’m testing a smaller register-file change: read each group of eight registers using the low address bits, then select the group with the high bits. This keeps storage and latency unchanged while reducing the read network’s decode and masking logic."}}
{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_45", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261002-002-r12s1.yaml')\nd={\n'id':'hyp-20261002-002-r12s1',\n 'title':'Bank-local register reads with late bank selection',\n 'category':'structural',\n 'motivation':'''The champion's reported worst path begins at fetch-queue occupancy and ends at an ID/EX rs2 operand register through the register file: 16.717 ns and ten cells. It scores 216.47 iter/sec at 87.715 MHz with 4,052,037 marked CoreMark cycles. The current RF groups registers into fours of eight, but it still decodes the full five-bit address and masks every word before reduction. Its physical read structure therefore places full-address decoding, wide word gating and reduction after the fetch-queue instruction mux. The r3s1 structural success established explicit flip-flop storage and validity-only decode squash; retain both. Prior carry-select arithmetic and small late-store cycle savings did not outperform the champion. A more compact RF read topology addresses the newly exposed operand path without another pipeline stage.''',\n 'hypothesis':'''Restructure each RF read port into four independent eight-word local read networks followed by late four-way bank selection. Keep the existing 31 writable 32-bit flip-flop words and x0 constant, one synchronous write port, synchronous reset, combinational read latency, and write-first bypass. This is one structural change to RF read organization; the five-stage pipeline, fetch queue, branch policy, M engines, source-tag matching and retirement boundary remain cycle-for-cycle unchanged.\n\nFor each port predecode rs_addr[2:0] into eight low selects and rs_addr[4:3] into four high selects. Mask each word only with its low select, so every bank independently computes the value at the same offset. Reduce those eight masked words with fixed balanced OR wiring. Only after each local eight-word reduction, mask that bank result by its high select, then combine the four bank results with a balanced reduction. High bank selects must not re-enter individual word masks or a full five-bit per-word select. Use fixed-index generated words and explicit wiring to retain flip-flop storage and avoid RAM/read-output register inference.\n\nIn particular, form local leaves as pairs of word-and-low-select terms. The Boolean function (word_even_bit & low_even_select) | (word_odd_bit & low_odd_select) has four inputs and fits a LUT4; high-select qualification is deliberately absent from these leaves. Reduce four pair results locally, then form two pairs of bank-and-high-select results and their final OR. This lets Gowin map shallow local reads and late bank selection with fewer masking LUTs and less distributed full-address control. Both source ports remain independent and can read any pair, including equal addresses, two different offsets within one bank, and different banks; no bank-conflict interlock is introduced.\n\nPreserve the external reg_file interface. Keep x0 priority, independent same-cycle WB bypass on both ports, write isolation, reset-over-write priority, all selected raw source-field values reported by RVFI, retained WB forwarding through dmem stalls, registered EX bypass selection, and validity-only ID/EX squash. Do not snapshot RF contents in fetch, delay reads, add general pipeline stages, remove any register initialization, or change instruction admission. Keep nret=1, the complete top-level core IO, decoder default-illegal behavior, every trap and memory bound, exact-once stores and register writes, contiguous retirement order, M arithmetic and ALTOPS, eight-edge division, and unchanged ready-high JALR and branch-to-divide latency checks. Modify no evaluation or formal contract.\n\nRetain all existing RF tests and verify all 1,024 address pairs against an independent architectural array, including every same-bank and cross-bank pair, x0, independent and simultaneous bypasses, all writable destinations, reset, and random mixed writes. Run unchanged pipeline/queue tests and the original single-retire formal suite. Compare complete selftest/random RVFI traces under ready-high and randomized buses, and validate canonical stalled CoreMark CRCs, validation text, memory bounds and marker-bracketed cycles. The intended marked cycle count is still 4,052,037.\n\nMeasure all three Gowin placements and inspect the RF mapped netlist for bank-local leaf functions, late high-select gating, unchanged storage FFs and zero RF BSRAMs. Qualification requires fitness above 226.42762 iter/sec, approximately 91.74931 MHz at unchanged cycles. The extra local-bank activity, shared low-select fanout, WB bypass, placement changes and remaining EX/divider paths are the principal timing risks. Expected benefit is a compact read topology and higher Fmax with unchanged CoreMark IPC. Prototype timing, rather than reduced RTL complexity alone, must determine whether this clears the 4.6 percent fitness gate.''',\n 'expected_impact':{'fitness_delta_pct':8,'confidence':'medium'},\n 'changes':[\n {'file':'rtl/reg_file.sv','description':'''Replace full five-bit per-word read qualification with independent eight-word bank-local low-select reductions and late high-select bank masking on both ports. Use explicit pair leaves and balanced reductions. Preserve the existing flip-flop storage, binary read ports, one write port, x0, write-first bypass, synchronous reset and read latency.'''\n },\n {'file':'test/test_reg_file.py','description':'''Keep every existing assertion and use an independent architectural RF model to cover all source pairs and same-bank/cross-bank aliases, isolated writes, simultaneous bypass on either/both ports, x0 priority, synchronous reset and seeded mixed reads/writes. Add directed coverage of all eight local offsets for each of the four banks.'''}]\n}\np.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(d,sort_keys=False,width=88,default_flow_style=False))\njsonschema.validate(yaml.safe_load(p.read_text()),json.load(open('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json')))\nprint('Updated schema-valid structural hypothesis',p)\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
