ine waits.\nEach queued payload holds its own PC, instruction, and the exact\npredicted_taken bit used for that acquisition. This is a single\npredictor-guided lookahead mechanism, with no new predictor training.\n\nImplement fou\nhyp-20261002-002-r11s1 structural Isolate branch recovery with speculative fetch and decode state\nH states, preferably mutually exclusive\none-hot flags. Reset selects HELD. An accepted redirect selects the\nappropriate recovery bank; otherwise storage_accept selects NEXT and\nno acquisition selects HELD. Every non-reset edge sets the whole token\nafresh, with redirect taking priority over acquisition.\n\nThe current architectural fetch address A is the token-selected bank,\nand drives io_imemAddr, predictor.pc and response.pc consistently.\nCompute next_pc from A and the unchang\nhyp-20261002-003-r11s2 predictor Registered prediction recovery with an indirect landing bypass\nion.\n\nDistinguish the immediate squash pulse from a direct resident-PC install\nand the registered indirect landing indication. Direct corrections still\nhave priority over ordinary acquisitions and install their registered\nalternate PC on the resolving edge. A JALR squash clears occupancy and\ninvalidates simultaneous wrong-path admission; it must not send its live\ntarget sum into the resident-PC data mux. The resident PC may make one\nharmless speculative acquisition on this sq\nhyp-20261002-002-r12s1 structural Two-bank operand delivery with queued source predecode\nvectors from IF directly into RF in core. ID still receives the original selected instruction/PC/prediction and current RF operands, and captures exactly as before. Preserve queue acquisition and flush rules, accepted ready/unready JALR landing behavior, direct recovery, load/multiply replay, retained WB bypass during stalls, eight-edge division, real M arithmetic and ALTOPS, decoder default-illegal rules, all traps, contiguous retirement and exact-once memory effects. Keep n\nhyp-20261002-003-r12s