les.\nIf the queue is full and decode holds, repeated ready responses overwrite\nonly the spare bank; occupied instructions cannot be corrupted. An empty\nfallthrough response may similarly leave an unreachable speculative copy.\n\nAdvance tail by one ring position only on the existing storage_enqueue;\nadvance head by one position only on the existing storage_pop. Retain the\nexisting storage_accept, storage_bypass, storage_enqueue and occupancy\ntransitions, so bus-PC advancement and queue availability remain identical.\nFor full pop/refill, capture into the pre-edge spare slot, advance both\npointers, and make the just-freed old head the new spare. With count zero,\nhead equals tail; empty bypass advances neither. Reset or accepted redirect\nclears occupancy and restores both pointers to bank zero, independently\nof speculative payload writes. Occupancy alone makes stale banks unreachable.\nThe physical fifth bank must NEVER become a fifth logical queue entry.\n\nQueued operand snapshots must stay coherent with actual committed RF\nwrites. Broadcast each nonzero WB write to all five banks, comparing the\ndestination independently with each bank's own registered instruction\nrs1 and rs2 fields. Refresh matching operand halves on that edge, even\nwhile decode is held. Raw-response capture has priority over refresh in\nthe tail bank and already includes the RF's existing write-first bypass.\nNever shift instruction or operand banks on a pop: only pointers move.\nUnreachable banks can be refreshed harmlessly, without count/valid gates.\nSnapshot both raw source fields, including unused instruction aliases;\nretain x0 zero from raw RF capture and exclude x0 from every WB snoop.\n\nFor dequeue, form each bank's coherent operand using a same-cycle WB\nmatch/bypass before head selection. Select the five registered payloads\nand five corrected operand pairs with fixed-index masked-OR balanced\nreductions driven solely by head one-hot bits. Then use count\"'!=0 to select\ncompleted queued operands or raw RF outputs. WB tag comparisons must be\nparallel per bank, independent of head/count, rather than following a\nselected tag. No new RF read network, architectural RF copy, pipeline stage,\nsource-predecode sidecar or target/direction cache is needed.\n\nWire raw imemData[19:15] and [24:20] directly to the existing RF ports;\nroute its raw results and actual WB write signals to IF; route IF'\"'s selected\ncoherent operands to ID. Keep selected instruction binary tags for hazards,\nregistered forwarding, x0 semantics and RVFI. Existing EX/MEM and MEM/WB\nbypasses cover older producers not yet committed on decode admission.\nWB snooping covers producers that commit while a consumer waits and leave\nthose bypass stages. Do not snoop speculative EX/MEM ALU values, which do\nnot contain available load or multiply results. Preserve retained WB\nforwarding during bus holds and divider waits.\n\nKeep BTFNT/aligned-JAL prediction, every fetch-PC acquisition rule,\noccupancy-only squash, direct recovery and ready/unready JALR landings.\nPreserve eight-edge division, MEM multiplication, real M arithmetic and\nALTOPS, nret=1 and every core port. Retain default-illegal decoding, all\ntrap/alignment checks, exact-once in-order retirement and memory effects,\ncontiguous RVFI order, memory bounds and every existing assertion and\nformal depth. Change no evaluator, wrapper, benchmark or core.yaml contract.\n\nValidate an independent architectural RF plus logical deque: on each\nadmission, both presented operands must equal the current write-first RF\nreads, regardless of acquisition age or physical bank index. Cover writes\nafter enqueue, repeated same-tag writes, either/both sources, x0, simultaneous\ncapture and snoop, all occupancies and pointer wraps, full holds/refills,\nreset, flush, changing unready bus data and indirect landings. Assert that\nthe tail bank is outside the occupied ring interval, both pointers are\none-hot, and count never exceeds four. Long ready/full/held sequences must\nleave occupied instructions and operands intact except legitimate WB refresh.\n\nRetain all pipeline tests and the ten-clock branch-to-divide retirement\nbound. Add aged consumers whose producers have committed and left bypass\nstages, same-tag consecutive writers, load/MUL/DIV producers, prolonged\nmemory/M-engine holds, immediate forwarded dependencies and wrong-path\nflushes. Run unchanged lint, unit, single-retire formal, complete stalled\nand unstalled selftest/random RVFI cosim, and canonical stalled CoreMark\nCRC/UART/bounds gates. Intended marked CoreMark cycles remain 4,052,037.\n\nMeasure all three Gowin placements. Qualification requires greater than\n226.42762 iter/sec or approximately 91.75 MHz at unchanged cycles. Extra\nstorage is 320 operand FFs plus one 66-bit spare payload and ten pointer\nFFs; RF storage and its two read trees remain shared. The larger head\nselection and WB broadcast are material routing risks. Confirm that wide\nbank acquisition enables depend only on ready and registered tail bits,\nand that occupancy no longer precedes RF reads. The expected gain is an\nestimate until vendor timing confirms it; all correctness gates must pass.\n'''\nd['changes'][0]['description']='''Replace four shifting payload banks with five stationary physical banks\nholding four logical entries and one spare. Add registered one-hot head/\ntail pointers, raw-ready speculative spare capture, WB-coherent operand\nsnapshots and balanced head selection. Keep original logical occupancy,\nfallthrough, bus acquisition and PC/recovery timing.\n'''\nd['changes'][2]['description']='''Retain independent deque and recovery assertions; add RF writeback\nfreshness checks at admission, ring/spare invariants and pointer-wrap\ncoverage. Exercise every occupancy, full ready holds/refills, both-source\nsnoops, repeated writes, x0, capture/write races, reset, redirects and\nready/unready indirect landings.\n'''\np.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(d,sort_keys=False,width=90))\njsonschema.validate(d,json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nprint('Updated complete structural hypothesis; schema valid')\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "Updated complete structural hypothesis; schema valid\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
