{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_59","type":"agent_message","text":"The stationary-bank version also lost timing, with the head selector now feeding the recovery-PC path. I’m checking a simpler structural alternative: replicated asynchronous LUT-RAM register-file storage, with per-register validity bits to preserve reset semantics. It could reduce both the RF read delay and routing load while keeping the pipeline unchanged."}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_60","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport shutil\np=Path('/srv/hwebench/tmp/555e5898/69cc8ea0/rf_ram_probe')\nshutil.copytree(Path.cwd()/'cores/bench/rtl',p/'rtl',dirs_exist_ok=True)\nshutil.copytree(Path.cwd()/'cores/bench/test',p/'test',dirs_exist_ok=True)\ns='''module reg_file (\n  input logic clock, reset,\n  input logic [4:0] rs1_addr, rs2_addr,\n  output logic [31:0] rs1_data, rs2_data,\n  input logic w_en,\n  input logic [4:0] w_addr,\n  input logic [31:0] w_data\n);\n  logic [31:0] valid_q;\n  wire [31:0] bank1_data [0:1];\n  wire [31:0] bank2_data [0:1];\n  always_ff @(posedge clock) begin\n    if (reset) valid_q <= 32'b0;\n    else if (w_en && w_addr \"'!= 0) valid_q[w_addr] <= 1'\"'b1;\n  end\n  for (genvar g=0; g<2; g++) begin : bank\n    (* syn_ramstyle = \\\"distributed_ram\\\" *) logic [31:0] mem1 [0:15];\n    (* syn_ramstyle = \\\"distributed_ram\\\" *) logic [31:0] mem2 [0:15];\n    always_ff @(posedge clock) begin\n      if (w_en && w_addr \"'!= 0 && w_addr[4] == 1'\"'(g)) begin\n        mem1[w_addr[3:0]] <= w_data;\n        mem2[w_addr[3:0]] <= w_data;\n      end\n    end\n    assign bank1_data[g] = mem1[rs1_addr[3:0]];\n    assign bank2_data[g] = mem2[rs2_addr[3:0]];\n  end\n  wire [31:0] rf1 = rs1_addr[4] ? bank1_data[1] : bank1_data[0];\n  wire [31:0] rf2 = rs2_addr[4] ? bank2_data[1] : bank2_data[0];\n  always_comb begin\n    if (rs1_addr == 0) rs1_data = 32'b0;\n    else if (w_en && w_addr == rs1_addr) rs1_data = w_data;\n    else if (valid_q[rs1_addr]) rs1_data = rf1;\n    else rs1_data = 32'b0;\n    if (rs2_addr == 0) rs2_data = 32'b0;\n    else if (w_en && w_addr == rs2_addr) rs2_data = w_data;\n    else if (valid_q[rs2_addr]) rs2_data = rf2;\n    else rs2_data = 32'b0;\n  end\nendmodule\n'''\n(p/'rtl/reg_file.sv').write_text(s)\nprint(p)\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
