tor, benchmark or\ncore.yaml contract, and retain every existing test assertion.\n\nRun existing exhaustive RF tests and add independently modeled sequences\nwith repeated resets after filling every register, all 1,024 source pairs,\nunwritten-versus-written reads, same/cross-bank sources, writes to x0,\nfirst post-reset WB bypass on either/both ports, reset coincident with WB,\nand random reads/writes/reset events. Check both copies indirectly by\nreading each written value on both ports. Run all pipeline tests including\nunused raw-field RVFI aliases, prolonged memory/M-engine holds, replay,\nbranch/JALR and the existing ten-clock branch-to-divide bound. Run unchanged\nsingle-retire formal and complete ready-high/stalled selftest/random RVFI\ncomparisons plus canonical CoreMark CRC/UART/bounds validation.\n\nThe intended stalled CoreMark cycle count is unchanged at 4,052,037.\nMeasure all three Gowin placements and require fitness above 226.42762\niter/sec, approximately 91.75 MHz at unchanged cycles. Nominal writable\nRF FF storage falls from 992 bits to 31 validity bits, at the cost of two\ncoherent RAM copies (about 2 Kbit total) and bank/bypass/valid selection.\nUse only resources inside the existing FPGA budget. The main risks are\nGowin mapping the arrays to FFs or BSRAM, distributed-memory routing, and\nvalid/bypass selection replacing the old RF timing bottleneck. The expected\ngain is an estimate until actual vendor timing and all correctness gates\nconfirm it.\n''',\n'expected_impact':{'fitness_delta_pct':8,'confidence':'low'},\n'changes':[\n{'file':'rtl/reg_file.sv','description':'''Replace explicit FF words and masked-OR read reductions with two\nidentically written asynchronous distributed-RAM copies, each split into\ntwo 16x32 banks. Add reset-cleared per-word validity, preserve x0 and\nsame-cycle WB priority, and retain the complete existing RF interface.\n'''},\n{'file':'test/test_reg_file.py','description':'''Preserve every RF assertion and exhaustive source/write coverage. Add\nrepeated-reset tests over previously filled RAM, unwritten reads, first\npost-reset write-first bypass, reset/write coincidence and randomized\nreference-model checks that exercise both replicated read ports.\n'''},\n{'file':'test/test_pipeline.py','description':'''Retain all pipeline/RVFI/M-engine/latency checks. Add repeated reset with\npreviously live RF values, both-port WB aliases, first-write dependencies,\nlong bus/M-engine holds and branch/JALR uses of replicated RAM values.\n'''}]}\np.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(d,sort_keys=False,width=90))\njsonschema.validate(d,json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nprint('Complete LUT-RAM structural hypothesis written and schema valid')\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "Complete LUT-RAM structural hypothesis written and schema valid\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
