ot 1 for v[0] AND NOT v[1], slot 2 for v[1] AND NOT\n  v[2], or slot 3 for v[2] AND NOT v[3]. When stall is false, append to\n  slot 0 for v[0] AND NOT v[1], slot 1 for v[1] AND NOT v[2], slot 2\n  for v[2] AND NOT v[3], or slot 3 for v[3]. Every append condition is\n  qualified by \n…[3441 of 6513 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:e214f0cf1959b013]…\nnary count control, append subtraction/indexing,\n      and empty/full comparisons with direct head/full bits and fixed\n      slot append conditions. Preserve payload movement, fallthrough,\n      capacity, PC acquisition, flush priority and both recovery paths.\n      Retain count_q only as an optional verification-only derived value.\n  - file: test/test_if_stage_queue.py\n    description: |\n      Retain the independent deque oracle and every existing acceptance,\n      payload, PC and recovery assertion. Check all five prefix-valid\n      encodings against deque length, exhaustive ready/hold transitions,\n      full replacement, empty bypass, flush priority and randomized runs.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: |\n      Preserve all architectural, RVFI, memory-effect and latency checks.\n      Update only occupancy observation plumbing if necessary and extend\n      queued/unready, load/MUL replay, divider holds, simultaneous bus\n      stalls and redirect/landing coverage to verify identical behavior.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
