ding in EX. No live EX result\n  or memory-read value is forwarded into decode.\n\n  EX forms each functional operand with fixed-index masked terms and a\n  balanced OR reduction. With four sources, each output bit has two\n  pairwise masked-OR leaves and one final OR, mapping natu\n…[4462 of 7534 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:9e4cdac4e16ef1b8]…\nw\n      functional source masks to ex_stage. Preserve all external ports,\n      stage acceptance, replay, write eligibility, and recovery wiring.\n  - file: test/test_ex_stage.py\n    description: |\n      Adapt fixture wiring for the functional masks and cover all legal\n      source choices, mixed raw/functional operand use, immediate aliases,\n      AUIPC, and held sources while retaining every existing assertion.\n  - file: test/test_id_stage.py\n    description: |\n      Adapt fixture wiring for decode-control outputs and verify their\n      association with the raw instruction across normal capture, hold,\n      and validity-only kill without relaxing existing pipeline checks.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: |\n      Add independent architectural regressions for mixed bypass sources,\n      youngest-writer priority, x0, raw immediate/AUIPC aliases, producer\n      traps, replay, prolonged stalls, and captured divide operands. Keep\n      RVFI, exact-once effects, and all existing latency assertions.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
