{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_3", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor line in open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'):\n d=json.loads(line)\n if d.get('category')=='predictor' or d['id']=='hyp-20261001-001-r10s0':\n  print(json.dumps({k:d.get(k) for k in ('id','title','fitness','cycles','fmax_mhz','critical_path','hypothesis')},indent=2))\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "{\n  \"id\": \"hyp-20261001-003-r1s2\",\n  \"title\": \"Small tagged next-PC predictor with two-bit branch hysteresis\",\n  \"fitness\": 13.26,\n  \"cycles\": 4208674,\n  \"fmax_mhz\": 5.579,\n  \"critical_path\": {\n    \"from\": \"cpu/u_id/id_ex_w.rs2_val_0_s100\",\n    \"to\": \"dmem_1_dmem_1_0_0_s\",\n    \"slack_ns\": -185.654,\n    \"arrival_ns\": 195.948,\n    \"logic_cells\": 147,\n    \"modules\": [\n      \"clock_ibuf\",\n      \"cpu/u_ex\",\n      \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu\",\n      \"cpu/u_ex\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"hypothesis\": {\n    \"motivation\": \"This core has no branch prediction: every taken conditional branch and every\\nJAL/JALR redirects from EX and discards the current fetch, even after a loop\\nor call site has executed many times. Its IF/ID bundle is combinational, so\\nthe actual penalty is one younger instruction slot per redirect, rather\\nthan the two-cycle penalty suggested by the five-stage comments. CoreMark's\\nrepeated loops and call sites can recover these slots with a small learned\\nnext-PC predictor. The measured critical path is through forwarding and\\nthe combinational M-extension ALU; a shallow predictor lookup is expected\\nto improve iterations/cycle without extending that arithmetic path.\\n\\nA reference-ISS profile of the canonical 2K, -O3, ten-iteration CoreMark\\nrun, bounded by its start/stop MMIO stores, counted 2,922,016 instructions,\\n529,588 conditional branches, 49,367 JALs, and 13,735 JALRs. The baseline\\nincurs 357,527 taken-control redirects. An architectural trace model of\\nthis 32-entry predictor produced 73,619 next-PC misses, saving 283,908\\ninstruction slots; against the recorded 4,491,485 stalled baseline cycles\\nthat corresponds to approximately 6.75% throughput gain at constant Fmax.\\nA 64-entry table improved that estimate only to 7.03%, making 32 entries\\nthe stronger area/timing tradeoff. This is a trace estimate, with immediate\\npredictor updates and without replaying pipeline stalls; it is not an RTL\\nsimulation or a measured FPGA improvement. The reference run matched all\\nfive canonical CRCs and the required UART validation t\n…[78076 of 81148 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:c1bf0091adcd2535]…\ndate forwarding, Boolean saturating transitions and a shallow cached-bit fetch lookup. Preserve B/J targets and legal/aligned control guards.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\",\n        \"description\": \"Wire predictor clock/reset and one accepted training event from existing registered EX/MEM PC, instruction, branch_taken and post-trap validity. Preserve every pipeline bundle, top-level port and retirement contract.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"file\": \"test/test_branch_predictor.py\",\n        \"description\": \"Retain exhaustive direct target, legality and alignment checks; add an independent history/counter/cache model for every state transition, same-context bypass, aliases, consecutive updates, holds and reset.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\",\n        \"description\": \"Preserve architectural assertions and check prediction state changes behind queued fetches, all hold reasons, loop exits, forward branches, RVFI continuity and absence of wrong-path stores.\"\n      }\n    ]\n  }\n}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
