ption, initialized strongly toward the\nobserved exception; do not replace a useful exception entry on an\nordinary static-correct branch. Invalidate a matching entry when its\ncounter reaches zero. Reset valid bits and pending-update validity;\npayload need not be reset because lookup always checks validity.\nDescribe storage as eight fixed flip-flop words with decoded write\nenables and a balanced masked-OR read, avoiding a target RAM or BSRAM.\n\nRegister the accepted EX update event, branch PC, and exception bit,\nand apply the cache update on the following edge. \n…[5484 of 8556 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:68086febe6b151b8]…\nowin Fmax. Update old bus-PC-hold observations to\nassert fetch-PC advancement only on accepted responses or corrections\nand full-queue holds, preserving every ID/EX hold, forwarding, retirement,\nreset and memory-effect assertion. Two original tests assume bus PC\nequals the blocked decode PC and must observe the head separately.\nThe main risks are added head-mux timing\ninto decode/RF and queue control placement. Measured RTL and FPGA results\nmust establish whether saved overlap exceeds the 4.6% acceptance margin.\n\nhyp-20261001-003-r7s2 Four-entry predictor-directed fetch lookahead MHz= 66.311 cycles= 4111263 fitness= 161.29\nhyp-20261001-003-r8s2 Prediction-guided fetch queue with validity-only recovery MHz= 73.936 cycles= 4111263 fitness= 179.84\nhyp-20261001-003-r9s2 Hashed static-agreement prediction from registered branch results MHz= 74.447 cycles= 4030475 fitness= 184.71\nhyp-20261001-003-r10s2 Cached local-history direction prediction with parallel bank training MHz= 78.453 cycles= 3959739 fitness= 198.13\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
