{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_57", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261002-003-r11s2.yaml'", "aggregated_output": "id: hyp-20261002-003-r11s2\ntitle: \"Preselected direct recovery PCs with registered JALR fallback\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  The champion scores 203.70 iter/sec at 82.542 MHz and 4,052,037 marked\n  CoreMark cycles. Its reported worst path runs from an ID/EX rs1 register\n  through EX to the fetch PC: 17.588 ns and 39 cells. Prediction recovery\n  still combines forwarded operands, target arithmetic, direction-dependent\n  target selection and the fetch-PC mux on one edge. The r9s2 agreement\n  table and r10s2 local-history table saved roughly two percent of cycles\n  but missed qualification after FPGA timing costs. A recovery-path change\n  directly targets the champion's current bottleneck without a table read\n  on every fetch. The existing reference profile counts only 13,735 JALRs\n  inside the CoreMark markers, versus 4.05 million measured cycles, making\n  one extra recovery cycle per JALR a small cost if it removes the full\n  forwarded JALR adder from the fetch-PC critical path.\nhypothesis: |\n  Implement one prediction-recovery architecture: preselect the alternate\n  PC for direct controls before EX, and register the operand-dependent\n  indirect recovery target before it can drive fetch. Preserve the current\n  stateless backward-taken/forward-not-taken and aligned-JAL predictor.\n\n  At the existing ID/EX capture edge, add a 32-bit direct_recovery_pc field\n  computed from the decode instruction's captured PC, decoded immediate\n  and exact captured predicted_taken: predicted taken selects wrapping\n  PC+4, otherwise select wrapping PC+immediate. Compute both candidates\n  in parallel before this registered selection. Preserve every low address\n  bit; do not assume arbitrary PCs or immediates are aligned. Append the\n  field above existing payload fields so their offsets remain stable.\n  Match the ID/EX reset and downstream hold, and keep kill/readiness as\n  validity-only controls. This field is recovery metadata, never RVFI's\n  architectural next PC.\n\n  For legal aligned direct branches/JAL, retain the existing\n…[5056 of 8128 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:e9ac119ae578224a]…\nash, pending interval and PC-install pulses to existing validity/queue controls while preserving top-level ports, forwarding and pipeline retirement.\"\n  - file: test/test_id_stage.py\n    description: \"Extend packed-field decoding and independently check alternate-PC capture, wrap, prediction association, validity-only kills, true holds and reset.\"\n  - file: test/test_ex_stage.py\n    description: \"Extend payload builders for the added field and test direct recovery target selection plus registered JALR acceptance, forwarding, alignment, stalls, reset and one-shot application.\"\n  - file: test/test_if_stage_queue.py\n    description: \"Check immediate indirect-recovery flush and pending acquisition suppression with empty/full queues and imem backpressure, preserving existing queue assertions.\"\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: \"Retain complete architectural and timing assertions; add forwarded JALR pending recovery, queued wrong paths, reset/backpressure and exact-once link/store/retirement cases.\"\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
