{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_9", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\np='cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'\nfor line in open(p):\n d=json.loads(line)\n if d.get('category')=='predictor':\n  print(d['id'],d['title'],'fitness',d.get('fitness'),'cycles',d.get('cycles'),'Fmax',d.get('fmax_mhz'))\n  if d['id'] in ('hyp-20261001-003-r9s2','hyp-20261001-003-r10s2','hyp-20261001-003-r2s2'):\n   h=d['hypothesis']; print(h['hypothesis'] if isinstance(h,dict) else h)\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20261001-003-r1s2 Small tagged next-PC predictor with two-bit branch hysteresis fitness 13.26 cycles 4208674 Fmax 5.579\nhyp-20261001-003-r2s2 Direction-only branch prediction with decoded direct targets fitness 87.61 cycles 4201740 Fmax 36.81\nAdd one compact, PC-indexed bimodal predictor with 64 two-bit saturating\ndirection counters. Read with fetch PC[7:2] and train with the resolving\nbranch's own PC[7:2]. Reset a per-entry initialized bitmap and interpret\nuninitialized entries as weakly not taken; leave the counter payload\nunreset for compact distributed-memory inference, and initialize it\nfrom that default on the first accepted update. Predict only\nlegal conditional BRANCH encodings with funct3 in {0,1,4,5,6,7}; obtain\ntheir target from the current instruction's B immediate plus fetch PC.\nPredict legal JAL instructions unconditionally using their J immediate\nplus fetch PC. JALR remains sequentially predicted and resolves in EX.\nSuppress taken predictions for targets misaligned to four bytes. There\nis no BTB, stored target, tag comparison, return stack, or global history:\ncounter aliases affect accuracy but cannot change instruction legality.\nImplement compact storage and a shallow lookup; avoid synthesizing a\nwide bank of target multiplexers or adding a pipeline stage.\n\nCarry the exact predicted next PC with each instruction through IF and\nID/EX. It must be the value used to advance fetch for that accepted\ninstruction, not a later lookup of a potentially updated counter.\nFetch advances to that prediction only when ID/EX admits the instruction.\nExisting load-use, imem, dmem, and divider waits hold PC and metadata.\nEX computes the existing architectural next PC, including PC+4 for the\nexisting misalignment/trap path. Compare this resolved next PC against\nthe carried prediction, and flush only on a mismatch. Correctly predicted\nbranches and JALs must admit the younger instruction without a bubble;\nboth taken-to-sequential and sequential-to-taken corrections must work.\nKeep RVFI pc_wdata tied to the resolved a\n…[8503 of 11575 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:f41dbca75adf1c83]…\n=1 ports, resolved architectural RVFI next PC and contiguous retirement.\n\nVerify all counter states against independent saturating integer arithmetic,\nevery history transition, same-context bypass, unchanged future-context\nselection, same-bank aliases, consecutive registered updates, no update on\nholds, reset, and cold static behavior. Retain exhaustive B/J target and\nreserved-encoding checks. Pipeline cases must combine changing predictor\nstate with queued instructions, loop exits, forward branches, every existing\nhold reason and wrong-path stores, checking full RVFI PCs, operands, order\nand exact-once memory effects. Run unchanged lint, formal and cosim gates,\ncanonical bracketed CoreMark CRC/UART/OOB validation and all three Gowin\nplacement options. Qualification requires fitness above 200.058 iter/sec;\nincreased FF placement density and cached-update routing are the main risks.\n\nhyp-20261002-003-r11s2 Registered prediction recovery with an indirect landing bypass fitness 216.47 cycles 4052037 Fmax 87.715\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
