{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_55", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261002-003-r12s2.yaml'", "aggregated_output": "id: hyp-20261002-003-r12s2\ntitle: \"Thermometer occupancy for the prediction-guided fetch queue\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  The current champion reaches 216.47 iter/sec at 87.715 MHz and\n  4,052,037 marked CoreMark cycles. Its reported worst path starts at\n  u_if/count_q[2], passes through fetch instruction selection and the\n  register file, and ends at ID/EX rs2_val: 16.717 ns, ten logic cells.\n  The prediction-guided four-entry queue hides fetch stalls, but its binary\n  occupancy requires decoding before selecting the instruction seen by\n  every decode consumer. The r9s2 agreement and r10s2 local-history tables\n  saved only about two percent of cycles and missed qualification after\n  routing costs. A faster representation of the existing speculative\n  queue attacks the measured predictor frontend bottleneck directly.\nhypothesis: |\n  Replace only the four-entry prediction-guided fetch queue's three-bit\n  binary occupancy with four registered thermometer bits v[3:0]. Legal\n  states are 0000, 0001, 0011, 0111 and 1111 for zero through four queued\n  responses. The instruction/head selector reads v[0] directly, and fetch\n  space availability reads !v[3] directly. Keep the existing stateless\n  backward-taken/aligned-JAL predictor, raw-response fallthrough, four\n  packed payload banks, acquisition policy and recovery topology.\n\n  Define pop=v[0]&&!stall, accept=imem_ready&&(!v[3]||pop),\n  bypass=!v[0]&&!stall and enqueue=accept&&!bypass. After a pop, retained\n  occupancy is s=pop ? {1'b0,v[3:1]} : v. When enqueue is true, the unique\n  append bank is identified by a hole boundary: e[0]=!s[0],\n  e[1]=s[0]&&!s[1], e[2]=s[1]&&!s[2], e[3]=s[2]&&!s[3]. Implement fixed\n  per-bank append enables using these Boolean expressions; remove the\n  binary subtract, variable append index and case decode. Shift banks on\n  pop exactly as before; append wins at its destination. Reset/redirect\n  must remain absent from payload write enables and data muxes.\n\n  On reset or accepted EX squash clear v to 0000. Otherwise, enqueue-only\n\n…[1985 of 5057 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:e695e41c3af8be6e]…\nPlacement and\n  remaining IF-to-register-file routing are the principal timing risks;\n  this is an unmeasured architectural estimate pending implementation.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 6\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: \"Replace binary count and append-index arithmetic with four thermometer occupancy registers, direct head/full controls and fixed Boolean append enables; preserve prediction-guided acquisition, payload writes and direct/indirect recovery latency.\"\n  - file: test/test_if_stage_queue.py\n    description: \"Extend the independent queue model to cover every thermometer transition, empty bypass, full pop/refill, holds, flush/reset and ready/unready indirect landings; retain content, prediction and PC association assertions.\"\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: \"Retain all RVFI, wrong-path-effect and latency checks; exercise all queue occupancies across load/M holds, bus stalls, direct direction misses and forwarded JALR landing recovery.\"\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
