{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_72", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261002-003-r12s2.yaml'", "aggregated_output": "id: hyp-20261002-003-r12s2\ntitle: \"Registered source predecode in the prediction-guided fetch queue\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  The champion reaches 216.47 iter/sec at 87.715 MHz and 4,052,037 marked\n  CoreMark cycles. Its reported worst path starts at u_if/count_q[2],\n  passes through fetch instruction selection and the register file, and\n  ends at ID/EX rs2_val: 16.717 ns, ten logic cells. Speculative fetch\n  lookahead hides bus stalls, but head-versus-raw instruction selection\n  puts occupancy ahead of register-address decoding. The r9s2 agreement\n  and r10s2 local-history predictors saved only about two percent of\n  cycles and missed qualification after routing costs. Make the existing\n  prediction-guided queue supply registered source predecode, so its\n  occupancy selects already decoded register sources.\nhypothesis: |\n  Add source predecode as sideband metadata to the four-entry\n  prediction-guided fetch queue. For every raw instruction independently\n  decode rs1[2:0] and rs2[2:0] into eight-bit one-hot low selects, and\n  rs1[4:3] and rs2[4:3] into four-bit one-hot high selects. Capture these\n  24 bits alongside each enqueued PC/instruction/prediction response.\n  Use four fixed 24-bit flip-flop banks, shifting on the existing\n  storage_pop and appending to exactly the existing append destination.\n  Append wins over shift. Source-mask banks, like instruction payload,\n  need no reset or recovery gate: flushed occupancy makes speculative\n  metadata unreachable. Preserve binary count, acquisition equations,\n  full pop/refill and empty fallthrough.\n\n  Export head availability, its raw five-bit rs1/rs2 fields and registered\n  24-bit source masks from IF. Wire these to RF independently of the\n  occupancy-selected IF/ID instruction. The RF ordinary source-address\n  inputs become the live instruction-bus rs1/rs2 fields. Decode their\n  low/high selects in parallel with the already registered head selects.\n  For word r, use select_rs1[r] =\n  (head_available && head_hi[r/8] && head_lo[r%8]) ||\n  (!head_availab\n…[3253 of 6325 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:2363a93aa8f5ef42]…\nrve one FF register bank, balanced read reductions, x0 and selected-source write-first bypass.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Wire head predecode and raw bus source fields to RF while retaining selected-instruction addresses for ID, hazards, forwarding and RVFI; preserve all top-level ports.\"\n  - file: test/test_if_stage_queue.py\n    description: \"Compare source masks with the independent deque's instruction fields through every occupancy, simultaneous shift/append, bus/hold case, flush/reset and indirect landing; retain content, PC and prediction assertions.\"\n  - file: test/test_reg_file.py\n    description: \"Preserve exhaustive address/write checks; cover both source paths, independent live addresses, predecode association, x0, WB bypass and selection transitions.\"\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: \"Retain all architectural and latency assertions; cover queued source association under load/M holds, bus stalls, branch correction and forwarded JALR landing without wrong-path effects.\"\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
