{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"agent_message","text":"The learned direction predictors saved only about 2% of CoreMark cycles, and the larger lookup and operand-read structures hurt timing. I’m focusing on the existing predictor-guided fetch queue: per-slot validity can remove the binary occupancy decode from the reported critical path without adding read ports or changing prediction behavior."}}
