{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_4", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg '\\\"category\\\":\\\\s*\\\"predictor\\\"|r13s2|r10s2|r9s2|r4s2|r2s2' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\"", "aggregated_output": "{\"id\": \"hyp-20261001-003-r1s2\", \"title\": \"Small tagged next-PC predictor with two-bit branch hysteresis\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"This core has no branch prediction: every taken conditional branch and every\\nJAL/JALR redirects from EX and discards the current fetch, even after a loop\\nor call site has executed many times. Its IF/ID bundle is combinational, so\\nthe actual penalty is one younger instruction slot per redirect, rather\\nthan the two-cycle penalty suggested by the five-stage comments. CoreMark's\\nrepeated loops and call sites can recover these slots with a small learned\\nnext-PC predictor. The measured critical path is through forwarding and\\nthe combinational M-extension ALU; a shallow predictor lookup is expected\\nto improve iterations/cycle without extending that arithmetic path.\\n\\nA reference-ISS profile of the canonical 2K, -O3, ten-iteration CoreMark\\nrun, bounded by its start/stop MMIO stores, counted 2,922,016 instructions,\\n529,588 conditional branches, 49,367 JALs, and 13,735 JALRs. The baseline\\nincurs 357,527 taken-control redirects. An architectural trace model of\\nthis 32-entry predictor produced 73,619 next-PC misses, saving 283,908\\ninstruction slots; against the recorded 4,491,485 stalled baseline cycles\\nthat corresponds to approximately 6.75% throughput gain at constant Fmax.\\nA 64-entry table improved that estimate only to 7.03%, making 32 entries\\nthe stronger area/timing tradeoff. This is a trace estimate, with immediate\\npredictor updates and without replaying pipeline stalls; it is not an RTL\\nsimulation or a measured FPGA improvement. The reference run matched all\\nfive canonical CRCs and the required UART validation text.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"This core has no branch prediction: every taken conditional branch and every\\nJAL/JALR redirects from EX and discards the current fetch, even after a loop\\nor call site has executed many times. Its IF/ID bundle is combinational, so\\nthe actual penalty is one younger instruction slot per redirect, rather\\nthan\n…[139477 of 142549 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:5e366a0eac849919]…\n suppression.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 202.95, \"delta_pct\": -6.25, \"vs_baseline\": 1574.5, \"fmax_mhz\": 81.152, \"ipc_coremark\": 3e-06, \"cycles\": 3998554, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 5924, \"ff\": 2161, \"seeds\": [81.063, 81.152, 81.152], \"perturbations\": [[0, 81.063, 14], [1, 81.152, 14], [2, 81.152, 14]], \"lutram\": 0, \"bsram\": 4, \"dsp\": 6, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_id/reg_q.rs1_val_2_s0\", \"to\": \"cpu/u_if/count_q_0_s1\", \"slack_ns\": -7.336, \"arrival_ns\": 17.63, \"logic_cells\": 39, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_fwd\", \"cpu/u_if\"]}, \"logic_levels\": 14, \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-02T00:29:30.469367Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 13, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-10-02 hyp-20261002-003-r13s2 (regression, -6.25%): Even a 48-bit, eight-bank predictor with cached agreement lookup can worsen operand/forwarding-to-fetch count_q timing, making a median Fmax drop from 87.715 to 81.152 MHz outweigh 1.32% fewer CoreMark cycles.\"}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
