{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"agent_message","text":"The learned direction tables saved only 1–2% of CoreMark cycles and lost timing. The more promising angle is prediction recovery: register the correction, then admit its target through a landing bypass while squashing the younger EX slot. This could remove branch comparison from fetch-queue control without adding a recovery cycle."}}
